hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"13801","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Khaythamah who said: I asked Ibn 'Umar: When do we perform witr? He said: We used to perform witr at the end of the night."
"13802","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer who mixes with people and restrains anger is greater in reward than the believer who does not mix with people nor endure their harm."
"13803","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt Abu Ya'la al-Tawwazi narrated, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated, from Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer who mixes with people and endures their harm is better than the believer who does not mix with people nor endure their harm."
"13804","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated, Sharik reported, from Abu Ishaq and Abu Hasin, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Ibn 'Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."
"13805","'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated, Shu'bah reported, from Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab who said: I asked Ibn 'Umar about ghusl on Friday? He said: We were commanded to do it."
"13806","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated, al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated, from Aban ibn Abdullah al-Bajali, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs: Ibn 'Umar did not pray before the 'Eid nor after it; he was asked about it? He said: I did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray before it nor after it."
"13807","Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Abu Mu'awiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in rank is a man who looks over his kingdom for two thousand years, seeing its farthest as he sees its nearest, looking at his wives, couches, and servants; and the highest of them in rank is one who looks at the Face of Allah twice every day."
"13808","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the hantamah. Shu'bah said: I said to Jabalah: What is the hantamah? He said: The jar."
"13809","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid narrated, from al-Shaybani, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The hantamah was forbidden. I said: And what is the hantamah? He said: The jar."
"13810","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated. And al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi narrated, saying: Shu'bah narrated, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The month is such and such: thirty and twenty-nine."
"13811","Abu Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated. And Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Ma'bad narrated, both saying: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever eats dates with a people, let him not take two together unless they permit him."
"13812","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Ziyad al-Tastari narrated, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated, from his father, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining dates together while eating."
"13813","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-'Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Amr al-Bajali narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining dates together unless a man seeks permission from his companions; if they permit him, let him eat as he wishes."
"13814","'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi and Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated. And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Hakam narrated, both saying: Shu'bah narrated, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining dates together unless a man seeks permission from his brother."
"13815","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated. And Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami narrated; both said: 'Umar ibn 'Ubayd narrated, Mis'ar narrated, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining dates together unless a man seeks permission from his companion."
"13816","'Ali ibn al-'Abbas al-Kufi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated, al-Ashja'i narrated, from Sufyan, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining two dates together."
"13817","'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Hamzah al-Marwazi narrated, Muhammad ibn Sallam narrated, 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated, from Abu Hamzah, from Raqabah, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade joining dates together."
"13818","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Hakam narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray inside the House, meaning the Ka'bah."
"13819","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn 'Uthman narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man al-Farra narrated, both saying: Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated, from his father, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar who said: A questioner asked about 'Ali? He said: About which matter of 'Ali do you ask? This is the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this is his house!"
"13820","Ahmad ibn al-Khadir ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdah al-Marwazi narrated, Abu Mu'adh al-Nahwi al-Fadl ibn Khalid narrated, Abu Hamzah narrated, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever of you prays, let him not spread his forearms as the dog spreads."
"13821","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Sha'tha 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Nafi' and Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Muslims stayed in Madinah for ten years offering sacrifice; he said: And that is the Sunnah."
"13822","'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever cleanses himself with stones, let him do so with three."
"13823","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-'Abbas al-Nasa'i narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated, Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated, from Qays ibn al-Rabi', from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade opening dates to see what is inside them."
"13824","Al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi narrated, both saying: Shu'bah narrated, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags a garment of his out of pride, Allah shall not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13825","'Ali ibn al-'Abbas al-Bajali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated, al-Ashja'i narrated, from Sufyan, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever drags his clothes out of arrogance, Allah shall not look at him."
"13826","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid reported, from al-Shaybani, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags a garment out of pride, Allah shall not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13827","'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Bahram narrated, saying: I found in the book of my father: from 'Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah shall not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13828","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated, my father narrated, Jabalah ibn Suhaym narrated, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah shall not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13829","'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Hamzah al-Marwazi narrated, Muhammad ibn Sallam narrated, 'Isa ibn Musa narrated, from Abu Hamzah, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever drags his clothes out of pride, Allah shall not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13830","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Jabalah narrated, Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated, from Shu'bah, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar who said: A man paid in advance for dates from a man of the Ansar, but they did not yield that year, so he disputed with him before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Has your palm borne fruit? He said: No. He said: Then for what do you consume his wealth?! So he ordered him to return it to him, and he forbade advance payment for palm trees until their ripeness appears."
"13831","Muhammad ibn 'Abdous ibn Kamil narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, al-Mas'udi narrated, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten of Ramadan."
"13832","Muhammad ibn Jaban al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan al-Razi narrated, al-Hakam ibn Bashir narrated, from 'Amr ibn Qays, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks the Night of Decree, let him seek it in the last ten."
"13833","'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ubaydullah narrated, Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated, Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated, from Mis'ar, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man afflicted with a chronic ailment, so he dismounted and prostrated; Abu Bakr passed by him and dismounted and prostrated; and 'Umar passed by him and dismounted and prostrated."
"13834","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Jarir narrated, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which places are best? And which places are worst? He said: The best of places are the mosques, and the worst of places are the markets."
"13835","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated, Za'idah narrated, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Beware of wrongdoing, for it is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"13836","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Hafs narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, Abu Hanifah narrated, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays 'Isha in congregation and prays four rak'ahs before leaving the mosque is like the equivalent of the Night of Decree."
"13837","'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from his father, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Judges are three: two judges in the Fire and one judge in Paradise: a judge who ruled by desire is in the Fire, a judge who ruled without knowledge is in the Fire, and a judge who ruled by truth is in Paradise."
"13838","'Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn 'Adi narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Furat narrated, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The false witness — his feet shall not move until the Fire becomes binding upon him."
"13839","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Furat narrated, from Muharib ibn Dithar who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while admonishing a man: Birds shall come on the Day of Resurrection beneath the Throne, lifting their beaks, striking with their tails, and casting out what is in their bellies, with no wrongdoing upon them — so beware of it (wrongdoing)."
"13840","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-'Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Amr al-Bajali narrated, Abu Maryam narrated, Muharib ibn Dithar narrated, saying: I heard Ibn 'Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the Muslim man is like the green tree whose leaves do not fall — and do you know which tree it is? Ibn 'Umar said: So I stood up, then I looked and found I was the youngest of the people; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the date-palm."
"13841","Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated, Warqa narrated, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise whose banks are of gold, water flows over pearls, its water whiter than milk and sweeter than honey."
"13842","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar, concerning the saying of Allah, exalted be His remembrance: ""Indeed We have granted you al-Kawthar"" — he said: A river in Paradise bordered with gold, its water flows over ruby and pearl, whiter than milk and sweeter than honey."
"13843","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me. And Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yusuf ibn 'Adi narrated, both saying: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated, from 'Asim ibn Kulayb, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for bowing, he would say takbir and raise his hands."
"13844","'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated, al-Mas'udi narrated, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten of Ramadan."
"13845","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' al-Kufi narrated, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach people the tashahhud upon the pulpit, as a teacher teaches children."
"13846","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah shall not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13847","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi narrated, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah shall not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"13848","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Kathir ibn 'Ubayd al-Hadhdha narrated, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated, 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid al-Wassafi narrated, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The general bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Prayer, and what your right hands possess — until he made it gurgle in his chest, and his tongue could no longer utter it."
"13849","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Kathir ibn 'Ubayd narrated, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated, 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid narrated, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most hated of the lawful to Allah is divorce."
"13850","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Kathir ibn 'Ubayd narrated, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated, from 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah named them the righteous because they were dutiful to fathers, mothers, and children; just as your parents have a right over you, so too your child has (a right)."
"13851","Muhammad ibn Aban al-Asbahani narrated to us, 'Ammar ibn Khalid al-Wasiti narrated, Qurrah ibn 'Isa narrated, from 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is imprinted upon every character except treachery and lying."
"13852","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq reported, Ibn Jurayj reported, 'Ata reported, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ruqba and no 'umra; whoever is given something as 'umra or ruqba, it is his for his life and his death. He said: Ruqba is to say: This belongs to the last of us to die; and 'umra is to grant it to him for his life by giving it for their lifetimes."
"13853","'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Suwayd al-Dhari' narrated, Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn 'Uthman narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is granted something as 'umra for his life, it is his after his death."
"13854","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated, from Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not practice ruqba; whoever is given something as ruqba, it is his; and do not practice 'umra; whoever is given something as 'umra, it falls into the path of inheritance."
"13855","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated. And Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Mazini narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated. And Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated, all saying: Abu al-Ahwas narrated, from Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a share in a slave guarantees his partners their portions."
"13856","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Khalid reported, from al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent women from the mosques, though their homes are better for them."
"13857","'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated, Hammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Himmani narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit al-Kahili, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting the month of Ramadan."
"13858","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Khayyat al-Makki narrated, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated, from Su'ayr ibn al-Khums and Mis'ar ibn Kidam, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"13859","Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mudrik narrated to us at the palace of Ibn Hubayrah, Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated, from Su'ayr ibn al-Khums, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten of Quraysh are in Paradise: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, 'Umar is in Paradise, 'Uthman is in Paradise, 'Ali is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Sa'd and Sa'id are in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf is in Paradise, and Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah is in Paradise."
"13860","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated. And al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated. And Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl narrated, Sharik narrated, from Fitr ibn Khalifah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: I grieve over nothing except that I did not fight the rebellious party alongside 'Ali."
"13861","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated, Sinan ibn Harun narrated, from Abdullah ibn Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from his father who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar say: I grieve over nothing that passed me by except fasting and prayer, my abandoning the rebellious party in not fighting it, and my absolving 'Ali of the pledge."
"13862","Al-Hasan ibn al-'Abbas and 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Raziyan narrated to us, both saying: Sahl ibn Zanjalah narrated, al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated, from Harun ibn 'Antarah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I broke fast one day of Ramadan? He said: Without excuse or illness? He said: Yes. He said: Evil is what you did! He said: Indeed; what do you command me? He said: Free a slave. He said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I have never owned a slave. He said: Fast two consecutive months. He said: I cannot. He said: Then feed sixty poor persons. He said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I cannot even feed my family. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket containing dates, and he said: Give this in charity. He said: To whom? He said: To the poorest you know. He said: By Him who sent you with the truth, there is no household between its two lava plains needier than us. He said: Then feed it to your dependents."
"13863","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ullawayh al-Qattan narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Isa al-'Attar narrated, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated, from Hafs ibn 'Imran al-Kindi, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to oil ourselves except every other day."
"13864","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ullawayh al-Qattan narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Siyabah al-Kufi narrated, 'Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no hamah."
"13865","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ullawayh narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Isa narrated, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated, from Hafs ibn 'Imran, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining two dates together."
"13866","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ullawayh narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Isa al-'Attar narrated, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated, from Hafs ibn 'Imran al-Kindi, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade splitting a date to see what is inside it."
"13867","Al-Hasan ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Umarah ibn Subayh al-Kufi narrated, Sahl ibn 'Amir narrated, 'Abbad ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No believer hates the Arabs, and no believer loves Thaqif."
"13868","Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn 'Abbad narrated, Abu Bakr al-Dahiri narrated, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer who mixes with people so they harm him, then endures their harm, is better than the believer who does not mix with people so they harm him yet endures their harm."
"13869","Khattab ibn Sa'd al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Ihab narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated, Abdullah ibn Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Makkah was made lawful for me for an hour of the day and was not made lawful for anyone after me; it is sacred by Allah's sanctity until the Day of Resurrection: its trees are not cut, its grass is not uprooted, its game is not startled, and its lost property is not picked up except by one who announces it. They said: Except idhkhir, for it is for our smiths and houses. He said: Except idhkhir."
"13870","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Murri reported, from al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: On the day 'Ali and Mu'awiyah met at Dumah al-Jandal, Hafsah said to me: It does not befit you to stay away from a reconciliation through which Allah reconciles the nation of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); you are the son-in-law of the Messenger of Allah and the son of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab. On that day Mu'awiyah came forward upon a great Bactrian camel and said: Who covets this affair, or hopes for it, or stretches his neck toward it? Ibn 'Umar said: I had never spoken to myself of worldly matters before that day, and I was about to say: He covets it who struck you and your father over Islam until he brought you both into it; then I remembered Paradise and its bliss and turned away from it."
"13871","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn 'Ali al-Bahili narrated, Abu Sufyan al-Himyari narrated, Hushaym narrated, from al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: A man of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews killed my brother. He said: I shall hand the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love; Allah shall grant victory at his hand and enable you over your brother's killer. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) aspired to it, so he sent for 'Ali and tied the banner for him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I am bleary-eyed as you see — and he was bleary-eyed that day — so he spat in his eye. 'Ali said: I never suffered bleary eyes after that day; then he went forth."
"13872","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali, nephew of Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah, narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Salim al-Sa'igh narrated, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit and Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The keys of the unseen are five; none knows them but Allah: rain — none knows it but Allah; with Him is knowledge of the Hour; no soul knows what it shall earn tomorrow; and no soul knows in which land it shall die."
"13873","Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Jabali narrated to us at Kufah, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Harithi narrated, 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-'Anqazi narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I wish to pledge to you for jihad. He said: Are your parents alive? He said: Yes. He said: Then strive in them."
"13874","'Allan ibn Abd al-Samad Maghammah narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn 'Umar: He was asked about the pregnant woman and the woman whose husband died? He said: We used to spend upon them."
"13875","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated. And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated. And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi narrated, all saying: Shu'bah narrated, from 'Uqbah ibn Hurayth who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the jarr, the gourd, and the muzaffat, and commanded that nabidh be made in skins. And the wording is Abu al-Walid's."
"13876","Al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from 'Uqbah ibn Hurayth, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The month is such and such — and he closed his thumb."
"13877","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, from Shu'bah, from 'Uqbah ibn Hurayth who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Night prayer is two by two; when you see dawn, perform witr with one rak'ah."
"13878","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Amr al-Ash'athi narrated, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, from Hibban ibn Abdullah, from 'Uqbah ibn Hurayth, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever seeks the Night of Decree, let him seek it in the last ten."
"13879","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashshar al-Nasa'i narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated, from Abdullah ibn 'Usm, from Ibn 'Umar who said: Washing a garment of urine was seven times; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept (reducing) until he made washing urine from a garment once."
"13880","Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated to us, my father narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abdullah ibn 'Usm, from Ibn 'Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: From Thaqif shall emerge a destroyer and a liar."
"13881","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated. And Musa ibn Harun and Muhammad ibn 'Abdous ibn Kamil narrated to us, both saying: 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated, both saying: Shu'bah narrated, from Hayyan al-Bariqi who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar say: Two rak'ahs of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are lighter than one rak'ah of your prayer."
"13882","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated, Hilw ibn al-Sari narrated, Abu al-Bilad narrated, saying: I heard Ibn 'Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Friday is obligatory except upon what you own or one with an ailment."
"13883","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to me, Sharik narrated, from Kulayb ibn Wa'il, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling dates until their ripeness appears."
"13884","Al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Mujawwiz al-Basri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated, Abu Raja al-Kulaybi narrated, Kulayb ibn Wa'il narrated, Abdullah ibn 'Umar narrated, saying: We used to declare the people of major sins doomed until this verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Indeed Allah does not forgive association with Him, but forgives what is less than that for whom He wills."" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to declare any of the monotheists doomed to the Fire."
"13885","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn Abd al-'Azim al-'Anbari narrated, al-Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated, Sinan ibn Harun al-Burjumi narrated, from Kulayb ibn Wa'il, from Ibn 'Umar who said: A trial was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a man passed by, and he said: This veiled one shall be killed therein, wronged. I looked and it was 'Uthman ibn 'Affan."
"13886","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated, 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi narrated, saying: I recited to Ibn 'Umar: ""Allah is He who created you from weakness, then made after weakness strength, then made after strength weakness."" Ibn 'Umar said: ""Allah is He who created you from weakness, then made after weakness strength, then made after strength weakness"" — thus I recited to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13887","Hafs ibn 'Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"13888","Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr narrated, from Fudayl, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"13889","Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Harun ibn Sulayman ibn Isma'il ibn Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman al-Sabbahi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated, Malik ibn Mighwal and Salih ibn Muslim narrated, both saying: 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi narrated, from Ibn 'Umar who said: I recited to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Allah is He who created you from weakness."" He said to me: ""From weakness,"" O my son."
"13890","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Ammar narrated, Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi who said: I recited to Abdullah ibn 'Umar: ""Allah is He who created you from weakness, then made after weakness strength, then made after strength weakness and gray hair."" Ibn 'Umar said: ""Allah is He who created you from weakness, then made after weakness strength, then made after strength weakness and gray hair."" Then Ibn 'Umar said: I recited it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you recited it to me, and he corrected me as I corrected you."
"13891","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated, Sawwar ibn Mus'ab reported, from 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi, from Ibn 'Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had him recite: ""Allah is He who created you from weakness, then made after weakness strength, then made after strength weakness."""
"13892","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar who said: A single prostration of these people is longer than three prostrations of the prostration of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13893","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated, from 'Atiyyah, Ibn 'Umar narrated to me, saying: This verse was revealed concerning the Bedouins: ""Whoever brings a good deed shall have ten like it."" A man said: What is for the Emigrants, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: What is better than that: ""Indeed Allah does not wrong an atom's weight; if it is a good deed He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward."""
"13894","'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi 'Umar al-'Adani narrated, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to recite: ""With that let them rejoice; it is better than what they gather."""
"13895","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Mis'ar narrated, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Night prayer is two by two; when you fear dawn, then one — or a single rak'ah."
"13896","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn al-Rabi' ibn Abi Rashid narrated, 'Amr ibn 'Atiyyah narrated, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar who said: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, so 'Umar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Command him to take her back, then let him divorce her afterwards if he wishes. He said: So he took her back and counted it as one."
"13897","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, saying: I found in the book of my father: from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ata, Nafi', and 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Maghrib and 'Isha with a single iqamah."
"13898","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, saying: I found in the book of my father in his handwriting: Ibn Abi Layla narrated, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is built upon five: upon testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan."
"13899","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi al-Tarsusi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is answerable for his flock."
"13900","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated, 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated, Abu Hamzah narrated, from Mutarrif, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no traitor but a banner shall be raised for him on the Day of Resurrection, and it shall be said: This is the banner of the treachery of so-and-so."
"13901","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Simmari al-Naqid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated, 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated, from Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari, from Mutarrif, from 'Atiyyah who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said... and he mentioned the same."
"13902","Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated, Sharik narrated, from Abdullah ibn 'Isa, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever does not show mercy shall not be shown mercy."
"13903","Al-'Abbas ibn Ibrahim al-Qaratis al-Baghdadi narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-'Anqazi narrated, 'Umar ibn Shabib al-Musalli narrated, from Abdullah ibn 'Isa, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of whomsoever I am his master, 'Ali is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."
"13904","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan narrated, 'Umar ibn Shabib narrated, from Abdullah ibn 'Isa, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The divorce of a slave woman is twice, and her waiting period is two menstruations."
"13905","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Baghdadi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from Hajjaj, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its ripeness appears."
"13906","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Sha'tha 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, Ash'ath, and al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar who said: I traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prayed with him at home and on journey: at home I prayed with him Zuhr four and two after it, 'Asr four with nothing after it, Maghrib three and two after it, 'Isha four and two after it, Fajr two with two before it. And on journey: Zuhr two with two after it, 'Asr two with nothing after it, Maghrib three with two after it, 'Isha two with two after it, Fajr two with two before it."
"13907","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated, Sawwar ibn Mus'ab narrated, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women have no share in going out except compelled — meaning she has no servant — except for the two 'Eids, al-Adha and al-Fitr; and they have no share in the roads except the edges."
"13908","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated, Mindal narrated, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn 'Atiyyah, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the wailing woman and the one who listens."
"13909","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn al-Rabi' ibn Abi Rashid narrated, 'Amr ibn 'Atiyyah narrated, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon his mount while riding."
"13910","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn al-Rabi' ibn Abi Rashid narrated, 'Amr ibn 'Atiyyah narrated, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gesture with his hand toward the east and say: Indeed tribulation is here, where the horn of Satan rises."
"13911","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn al-Rabi' ibn Abi Rashid narrated, 'Amr ibn 'Atiyyah narrated, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The month is twenty-nine."
"13912","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn al-Rabi' ibn Abi Rashid narrated, 'Amr ibn 'Atiyyah narrated, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Your parable and the parable of the Jews and Christians is like a man who hired workers and said: Who will work for me until midday for a qirat? So the Jews worked. He said: Who will work for me from midday until 'Asr prayer? So the Christians worked. He said: Who will work for me from 'Asr prayer until sunset for two qirats each? And you are they. The Jews and Christians worked and said: What is it with us — more work yet less reward? He said to them: Did I wrong you of anything? They said: No. He said: Did I not give you what I stipulated for you? They said: Yes. He said: That is My bounty, I grant it to whom I will, and Allah is Possessor of great bounty. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed your term among the terms of the nations that passed is as what remains from 'Asr prayer until sunset."
"13913","'Ali ibn Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Kathir ibn Jumhan who said: I saw Ibn 'Umar walking in the belly of the valley channel, and I said: You walk while you command people to hasten?! Ibn 'Umar said: If I walk, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walk — or 'Umar; and if I hasten, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hasten — or 'Umar."
"13914","Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated, Zuhayr narrated, from 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Kathir ibn Jumhan: A man said to Abdullah ibn 'Umar in the course between al-Safa and al-Marwah: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, why do I see you walking while people hasten? He said: If I walk, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walk; and if I hasten, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hasten — and I am an old man."
"13915","'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn 'Abs al-Tanukhi narrated, Yahya ibn Ya'la al-Aslami narrated, Abu al-Sabbah al-Wasiti narrated, from Abd al-'Aziz ibn Hakim al-Hadrami, from Abdullah ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to 'Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except there is no prophethood and no inheritance."
"13916","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Musa ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated, Sulayman ibn Abdullah ibn Wahb al-Kufi narrated, from Abd al-'Aziz ibn Hakim, from Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of ""there is no god but Allah"" suffer no loneliness in death, nor in graves, nor in resurrection; as if I see them at the Blast shaking dust from their heads, saying: ""Praise be to Allah who removed grief from us."""
"13917","Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated, al-Hasan ibn 'Ullawayh al-Qattan narrated, 'Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated, both saying: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Qasim ibn 'Awf al-Bakri who said: I heard Ibn 'Umar say: We lived a period of our time thinking this verse was revealed concerning us and the two People of the Book before us: ""Indeed you shall die, and indeed they shall die; then on the Day of Resurrection you shall dispute before your Lord"" — the verse. We said: How shall we dispute when our Prophet is one and our Book is one? Until I saw some of us striking the faces of others with the sword, and I knew it was revealed concerning us."
"13918","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to me, my father narrated, Shu'bah narrated, from 'A'idh ibn Nasib, who heard Ibn 'Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the Ka'bah."
"13919","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated, from 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam, Abu Malik al-Ashja'i reported, Husayn ibn al-Harith al-Jadali — Jadilah Qays — said: The governor of Makkah addressed us and adjured the people, saying: Who saw the crescent on such-and-such day? Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon us to perform the rites upon sighting; if we do not see it and two just witnesses testify, we perform the rites upon their testimony. I asked al-Husayn: Who is the governor of Makkah? He said: Al-Harith ibn Hatib, brother of Muhammad ibn Hatib. Then the governor said: Among you is one more knowledgeable of Allah and His Messenger than I, and he witnessed this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — gesturing with his hand toward a man. Al-Husayn said: I said to an elder beside me: Who is this to whom the governor gestured? He said: This is Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he is more knowledgeable of Allah and His Messenger than he. So we came to Ibn 'Umar, and he said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us."
"13920","Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, Salim Abu Abdullah al-Barrad narrated to me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it, he has a qirat. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how much is a qirat? He said: Like Uhud."
"13921","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Sharik from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr who said: Al-Sha'bi used to narrate the maghazi (military campaigns), and Ibn Umar passed by and heard him narrating them, and said: He is more retentive of them than I, though I witnessed them with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13922","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Sulayman ibn Harb from Shu'ba from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Sa'id ibn Amr from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are an unlettered nation; we neither write nor calculate. The month is such and such and such, and he closed his thumb on the third (gesture, i.e. twenty-nine days)."
"13923","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani from Ishaq ibn Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Sa'id from his father from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"13924","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Ghassan al-Nahdi Malik ibn Isma'il from Ishaq ibn Sa'id from his father Sa'id ibn Amr who said: We set out with Ibn Umar on the day of departure (yawm al-sadar, leaving Mina) until, when we were at the Jamra near al-Aqaba, a Yemeni caravan of pilgrims passed by us, their saddles of leather and their camels' halters of twisted rope, and he said: Whoever wishes to see the caravan most resembling the one that came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and those who came with him that year, let him look at this caravan."
"13925","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya ibn al-Himmani, both saying: Narrated Ishaq ibn Sa'id from his father from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a beast be made a target (bound and shot at). Al-Himmani added in his narration: And he said: If you wish to slaughter it, then slaughter it."
"13926","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban from Khalid ibn Sa'id from Amr ibn Sa'id from his father from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"13927","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf al-Ammi from Hafs ibn Ghiyath from Layth from Abu Muhammad who said: I accompanied Ibn Umar for a month, and I heard him reciting in the two rak'as of Fajr: Say, O disbelievers (Surat al-Kafirun) and Say, He is Allah, the One (Surat al-Ikhlas); and he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite them."
"13928","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani from Qays ibn al-Rabi', and narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Musa ibn A'yan, both from Layth from Sa'id ibn Amir from Ibn Umar who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we stopped at a pool containing water, and we drank directly from it with our mouths, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not drink directly from it with your mouths; rather wash your hands and drink in them, for there is no vessel more wholesome or cleaner than it. The wording is that of the narration of Qays ibn al-Rabi'."
"13929","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi from Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman who said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysara, from Abu Hariz, that Nufay' narrated to him from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a woman of Khath'am and said: How do you find yourself? She said: I see myself only (facing) what ails me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I would wish that you do not leave this world until you take charge of an orphan or equip a warrior."
"13930","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Asim al-Wasiti from Abu Tumayla from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Yahya ibn Yazid from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa from Nufay' ibn al-Harith from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for twenty nights reciting in the two rak'as before the dawn (Fajr) prayer: Say, O disbelievers and Say, He is Allah, the One. He said: And I heard him say: Excellent are the two suras: Say, He is Allah, the One equals a third of the Qur'an, and Say, O disbelievers equals a quarter of the Qur'an."
"13931","Narrated Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Shihab ibn Shurnufa al-Mujashi'i who said: I heard Abu Dawud al-Darimi say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar say: I observed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for twenty-four or twenty-five mornings as he prayed the two rak'as before the morning prayer, reciting in the first of them Say, O disbelievers and in the second: Say, He is Allah, the One."
"13932","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani from al-Salt ibn al-Hajjaj from al-Sabbah from Abu Dawud from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the evening of Arafah, no one remains in whose heart is a mustard seed's weight of faith but that he is forgiven. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people of Arafah specifically? He said: Rather for the Muslims generally."
"13933","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nu'aym from Isa ibn Qirtas from Abu Ja'far, freedman of Banu Hashim, who said: We were sitting with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said to him: What do you say about sweet lawful date-wine (tila')? We laughed and felt shy when he said lawful, so Ibn Umar said: I neither drink it nor give it to drink to anyone of my household. Abu Ja'far then said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention anything about these drinks? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding (vessels of) al-muzaffat, al-dubba' and al-naqir, and he said: Every intoxicant is unlawful. I said to him: Does nabidh intoxicate? He said: This is what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say."
"13934","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Mahdi ibn Maymun from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub from Ibn Abi Nu'm who said: I was with Ibn Umar when a man asked him about the blood of a gnat. He said to him: From where are you? He said: From the people of Iraq. He said: Look at this one! He asks me about the blood of a gnat while they killed the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: They (al-Hasan and al-Husayn) are my two sweet basils of this world."
"13935","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nu'aym from Abu Janab al-Kalbi from Hani' ibn al-Hadrami who said: We accompanied Ibn Umar with a group of the people of Kufa and Basra to follow his Hajj. When he poured forth from Arafat and came to Muzdalifa (Jam'), he established the prayer, and we prayed Maghrib with him; then he greeted (finished), then stepped forward and prayed two rak'as, and we thought he was offering voluntary glorification (extra prayer), until when he finished he walked to his tent, cast off his cloak and loosened his lower garment, then was given a coarse garment, came to his bedding and lay down on it. We said: What is expected of Ibn Umar, he has come to his bedding and lain down! So we went to him and said: The people are waiting for you to lead them in Isha prayer. He said: As the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, I have prayed. So we knew that the two rak'as were the obligatory (Isha, shortened and combined) prayer. Then he lay down, and when the people departed to go to Mina in the morning, he came out and prayed at length, then sat and said to his boy: Look, has the cluster of stars risen over the mountain? His boy said: Yes, it has risen. So he called for the prayer and prayed two rak'as, then established the prayer and we prayed with him, then he rode to the imam to pour forth with him."
"13936","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, both saying: Narrated Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani from Abd al-Salam ibn Harb from Ziyad ibn Khaythama from Nu'man ibn Qirad from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given the choice between intercession and that half of my nation enter Paradise, so I chose intercession, for it is more comprehensive. Yet it is not for the believing God-fearing; rather it is for the sinful, erring, defiled ones."
"13937","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Saffar from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi A'isha Abu Mu'awiya from Subayh, an old shaykh of ours, who said: Abd Allah ibn Umar came to us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep to sheep, for they are among the beasts of Paradise; pray in their resting place and wipe their nasal mucus. I said to him: What is al-ru'am? He said: Mucus."
"13938","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Mu'awiya ibn Amr from Za'ida from Kulayb ibn Wa'il from Habib ibn Abi Mulayka, known as Abu Thawr, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and asked him, saying: Tell me about Uthman: did he witness Badr? He said: No. He said: Did he turn away on the day the two hosts met (Uhud)? He said: Yes. He said: Did he witness the Pledge of Ridwan? He said: No. Then the man left, and a man said to Ibn Umar: This one will go and claim that you disparaged Uthman! He said: Did I? Bring the man back to me; so he was brought back, and Ibn Umar said to him: Did you understand what I said to you? He said: Yes. He said: As for the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, Uthman is engaged in Your need and the need of Your Messenger, so he allotted him a share (of the spoils). As for the day the two hosts met, Allah has pardoned him, saying: Those of you who turned back (Qur'an verse). As for the Pledge of Ridwan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to the confederates regarding the sacrificial animals, to make a truce and peace with us, but they refused; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, Uthman is engaged in Your need and the need of Your Messenger, and I pledge allegiance on his behalf; and he struck one of his hands upon the other. Go and strive your utmost against me (i.e. do your worst in misquoting me)."
"13939","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ghudani from Abd al-Rahman ibn Dhakwan, his maternal uncle, who said that he asked Abd Allah ibn Umar about nabidh. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-hantam and al-muzaffat, and commanded us to drink from that which is tied and hung (i.e. waterskins)."
"13940","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Asim ibn Ali from Qays ibn al-Rabi' from Iyad ibn Laqit from Abd al-Rahman ibn Nu'aym, brother of Banu al-A'raj, who said: A man came on the evening of Arafah to Ibn Umar and asked him, and Ibn Umar said: We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there is the Dajjal (Antichrist), and before the Dajjal there are thirty or more liars. We said: What is their sign? He said: That they come to you with a practice you were not upon, altering thereby your practice and your religion; so when you see them, avoid them and oppose them."
"13941","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Asim ibn Ali from Qays ibn al-Rabi' from Zuhayr ibn Abi Thabit from Tamim ibn Salama who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took suhur (predawn meal) one night with people at his place, and Alqama ibn Ulatha al-Amiri came, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invited him to a head (of meat), and Bilal came to call the prayer, so he said: Gently, O Bilal; let Alqama take suhur."
"13942","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nu'aym from Abu Janab from his father who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take a dinar for two dinars, nor a dirham for two dirhams, nor a sa' for two sa's; I fear usury for you. A man said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, a man buys a fine camel for (several) camels, and a horse for horses? He said: There is no harm in that when it is hand to hand."
"13943","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Dirar ibn Surad from Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Salim ibn Abi Hafsa from Jumay' ibn Umayr from Ibn Umar that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched Ali to Khaybar, he tied a banner for him and handed it to him."
"13944","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Asbahani from Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali from Ali ibn Salih from Hakim ibn Jubayr from Jumay' ibn Umayr from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ali is my brother in this world and the Hereafter."
"13945","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Asbahani from Isma'il ibn Umar al-Bajali from Qays ibn al-Rabi' from al-Jahhaf from Jumay' ibn Umayr from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between the people until none remained except Ali, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my brother? He said: You are my brother in this world and the Hereafter."
"13946","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat al-Qazzaz from Amr ibn Thabit from Abu al-Jahhaf and Kathir al-Nawwa', both saying: Narrated Jumay' ibn Umayr who said: I said to Abd Allah ibn Umar: Narrate to me about Ali. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) establishing brotherhood between the believers, and I heard him (Ali) say: O Prophet of Allah, all of them return with a brother except me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are you not pleased that I be your brother? He said: Yes. He said: Then I am your brother in this world and the Hereafter. Kathir said: I said: O Jumay', by Allah besides whom there is no god, did you hear it from Abd Allah ibn Umar?! So he swore three times that he heard it from Abd Allah ibn Umar."
"13947","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat al-Qazzaz from Amr ibn Thabit from Abu al-Jahhaf and Kathir al-Nawwa', both saying: Narrated Jumay' ibn Umayr who said: I said to Abd Allah ibn Umar: Narrate to me about Ali. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Khaybar say: I shall give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love. It is as if I see it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as he embraces it, while Ali ibn Abi Talib had sore eyes from the smoke of the fortress; so he handed it to him, and, by Allah, the horses had not yet fully assembled before Allah opened (granted victory of) it at his hands."
"13948","Narrated Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad from Sadaqa ibn Sa'id al-Hanafi from Jumay' ibn Umayr al-Taymi who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar say: We were at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awaiting him; he came out and we followed him until he came to a pass of the passes of Madinah and sat upon it, and said: O people, let none of you meet a caravan (to buy goods before it) nor let a migrant sell for a Bedouin; whoever buys a she-camel whose milk has been held back (muhafalla) has the option for three days: if he returns her, he returns with her a like amount, or he said: double her milk, of wheat."
"13949","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Yahya al-Himmani from Sharik from Abd Allah ibn Sharik who said: I performed Hajj as tamattu', and I asked Ibn Umar, Ibn Abbas and Ibn al-Zubayr, and they said: You have been guided to the practice of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): stand, circumambulate the House, then exit ihram."
"13950","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Mu'awiya ibn Amr from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari from Sufyan from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Yazid ibn Bishr al-Saksaki from Ibn Umar who said: Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting Ramadan, then jihad thereafter is good. Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us."
"13951","Narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn Zanbur from Fudayl ibn Iyad from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Yazid ibn Abi Bashir al-Saksaki who said: I met Ibn Umar, and he said: Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, establishing prayer, giving zakat, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan; and jihad and charity are of righteous deeds. Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us."
"13952","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi from Shu'ba from Amr ibn Murra from Abu al-Bakhtari who said: I asked Ibn Umar about money exchange (sarf). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling silver on credit for cash."
"13953","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Sulayman ibn Harb, both saying: Narrated Shu'ba from Amr ibn Murra who said: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari say: I asked Ibn Umar about advance payment (salam) for date-palms. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling the fruit until it emerges (ripens)."
"13954","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Sulayman ibn Harb from Shu'ba from Amr ibn Murra from Abu al-Bakhtari who said: I heard Ibn Umar about selling date-palms, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling date-palms until their soundness appears."
"13955","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani from Sa'id ibn Zakariyya from Anbasa ibn Abd al-Rahman from Muhammad ibn Rustum who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith without deeds is not accepted, nor deeds without faith."
"13956","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Zayd ibn al-Harish from Abd Allah ibn Khirash from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi' from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever calls people to a saying or deed and does not himself act upon it remains in Allah's displeasure until he desists or acts upon what he said or invited to."
"13957","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Zayd ibn al-Harish from Abd Allah ibn Khirash from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab from Ibrahim al-Taymi from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear a white cap (qalansuwa)."
"13958","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Zayd ibn al-Harish from Abd Allah ibn Khirash from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab from Ibrahim al-Taymi from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon every Muslim is hearing and obedience in what he loves and dislikes, so long as he is not commanded with disobedience to Allah."
"13959","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Zayd ibn al-Harish from Abd Allah ibn Khirash from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab from Ibrahim al-Taymi from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of religion is scrupulous piety (wara'), and the best of worship is understanding (fiqh)."
"13960","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Zayd ibn al-Harish from Abd Allah ibn Khirash from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab from Ibrahim al-Taymi from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever swears by other than Allah has committed shirk (association)."
"13961","Narrated Musa ibn Zakariyya al-Tustari from Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni from Isa ibn Yunus from Badr ibn al-Khalil from Ammar al-Duhni from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Ibn Umar that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting. He said: The white days, three days of every month."
"13962","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati from Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Samti from Abd Allah ibn Zayd al-Himsi from al-Awza'i from Abda ibn Abi Lubaba from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has people whom He singles out with blessings for the benefit of His servants; He leaves them therein so long as they expend them, and if they withhold them He strips them from them and transfers them to others."
"13963","Narrated Ubayd al-Ijl from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Thalj from Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith from Shu'ba from Za'ida ibn Umayr who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the House (Ka'ba), and there will come one who will forbid you from it, and you will hear from him; and Ibn Abbas was sitting."
"13964","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi from Abu Awana from Mansur from Abd Allah ibn Murra from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you loves a servant (of Allah), let him inform him, for he will find the like of what he finds for him."
"13965","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from Mansur from Abd Allah ibn Murra from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from vows, saying: It does not bring anything forward; rather it is extracted thereby from the miserly."
"13966","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Amr ibn Marzuq from Shu'ba from Mansur from Abd Allah ibn Murra from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade vows, and mentioned the like thereof."
"13967","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Abu Awana from Mansur from Abd Allah ibn Murra from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A vow does not avert anything, but it is extracted thereby from the miser."
"13968","Narrated Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dulabi, and narrated Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi from Ali ibn al-Ja'd from Sharik from Mansur from Abd Allah ibn Murra from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade vows and commanded fulfilling them."
"13969","Narrated Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i from Muhammad ibn Rafi' al-Naysaburi from Yahya ibn Adam from Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil from Mansur from Abd Allah ibn Murra from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade vows, and mentioned the like thereof."
"13970","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nu'aym from Mis'ar ibn Kidam from Wabara who said: I asked Ibn Umar: When do I stone the jamarat? He said: When your imam stones, then stone. I repeated the question to him, and he said: We used to watch for the time, and when the sun declined we stoned."
"13971","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nu'aym from Mis'ar ibn Kidam from Wabara from Ibn Umar who said: He appointed for the people of Yemen Yalamlam, for the people of Madinah Dhu al-Hulayfa, for the people of Syria al-Juhfa, and for the people of Najd Qarn as miqat. I mentioned Iraq to him, and he said: There was then neither Kufa nor Basra."
"13972","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nu'aym from Mis'ar from Wabara who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The muhrim (pilgrim in ihram) kills the kite, the vicious dog, the wolf, the mouse and the crow. I mentioned to him the snake and the scorpion, and he said: It is indeed said so."
"13973","Narrated al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Dallal al-Kufi from Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari from Abd Allah ibn Mis'ar ibn Kidam from his father from Wabara from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Be clean and be cautious."
"13974","Narrated Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Shami al-Kufi from Abu Kurayb from Mu'awiya ibn Hisham from Muhammad ibn Jabir from Abu Ishaq from Wabara from Ibn Umar who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than twenty times reciting in the two rak'as before Fajr: Say, O disbelievers and Say, He is Allah, the One."
"13975","Narrated Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Qattan, both saying: Narrated Yusuf ibn Adi from Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from Wabara ibn Abd al-Rahman who said: I said to Ibn Umar: May I circumambulate the House while in ihram? He said: What prevents you? He said: Ibn Abbas used to forbid that until the people return from al-Mu'arraf (Arafat/Muzdalifa). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj and circumambulated the House and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwa; so the practice of Allah and the practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more deserving to be followed, or the practice of Ibn Abbas, if he was truthful?!"
"13976","Narrated Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi from al-Hasan ibn Arafa from Qudama ibn Shihab al-Mazini from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from Wabara from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which earning is purest? He said: A man's work with his hand, and every righteous sale."
"13977","Narrated Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi from Abu Humayd Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira ibn Sayyar al-Himsi from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar from Hafs ibn Sulayman from Muhammad ibn Suqa from Wabara ibn Abd al-Rahman from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, indeed wards off affliction from a hundred households of his neighbors through a righteous Muslim; then Ibn Umar recited: Were it not for Allah repelling people, some by others, the earth would be corrupted."
"13978","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Hafs ibn Ghiyath from Layth from Umayr ibn Abi Umayr from Ibn Umar who said: I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasting on a Friday at all."
"13979","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn A'yan al-Baghdadi from Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi from Asbat ibn Muhammad from al-A'mash from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah from Sa'd, freedman of Talha, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a narration which, had I heard it only once or twice until he counted seven times, but I heard it more than that; he said: There was al-Kifl among the Children of Israel who did not refrain from any sin he committed; a woman came to him and he gave her sixty dinars to have intercourse with her, and when he sat with her as a man sits with his wife, she trembled and wept. He said: What makes you weep? Did I compel you? She said: No, but this is a deed I have never done; only need drove me to it. He said: You do this though you never did it? Then he got down and said: Go, and the dinars are yours; then he said: By Allah, al-Kifl shall never disobey Allah again. He died that night, and by morning it was written upon his door: Allah has forgiven al-Kifl."
"13980","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from Yazid ibn Mihran Abu Khalid al-Khabbaz from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash from al-A'mash from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah al-Razi from Sa'id, freedman of Talha, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than twenty times say: A woman came to Dhu al-Kifl; when he drew near her she wept, and he withdrew aside; death came to him in the night, and by morning it was written upon his door, written: Allah has forgiven you."
"13981","Narrated Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi from Dawud ibn Mikhraq al-Firyabi from Abd Allah ibn Idris from Ibn Mighwal and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from Abu Hanzala who said: I asked Ibn Umar about prayer while traveling. He said: Two rak'as. I said: We are secure, we do not fear! He said: The practice of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13982","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father from Muhammad ibn Ja'far from Shu'ba from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid who said: I heard Hakim al-Hadhdha' say: I heard Ibn Umar asked about prayer while traveling. He said: Two rak'as; the practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"13983","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Jandal ibn Waliq from Mindal from Abu Hazim from Umar al-Azdi from Umayr ibn Hisham from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Hell has seven gates, and one gate thereof is for whoever draws a weapon against my nation."
"13984","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah from Sa'd ibn Ubayda from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The month is such and such, and he held back his thumb."
"13985","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Mu'awiya ibn Amr from Za'ida from Abu Husayn from Sa'd ibn Ubayda who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and asked him about Ali, so he mentioned his best deed, then said: That is his house, the middlemost of the houses of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or the middle of the houses of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — Abu Husayn doubted — then Ibn Umar said to him: I see it displeases you?! He said: Yes. Ibn Umar said: May Allah distance you and abase your nose; then he said: Leave."
"13986","Narrated al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Zawlaq al-Misri from Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash from Abu Husayn from Sa'd ibn Ubayda from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Night prayer is two by two; when you fear dawn, pray odd (witr) with one."
"13987","Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Asim ibn Ali from Sharik from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah from Sa'd ibn Ubayda from Ibn Umar that he heard a man say: By the Ka'ba! He said: Woe to you! Do not say: By the Ka'ba, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every oath sworn by other than Allah is shirk."
"13988","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from his father, Mansur and al-A'mash, from Sa'd ibn Ubayda from Ibn Umar who said: Umar used to swear by his father, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him, saying: Whoever swears by anything besides Allah has committed shirk."
"13989","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi from Ali ibn al-Ja'd from Sharik from Jabir from Sa'd ibn Ubayda from Ibn Umar that he heard a man say: By the Ka'ba! He said: Do not say: By the Ka'ba, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every oath sworn by other than Allah is shirk."
"13990","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili from Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' from Ja'far ibn Maysara from his father from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever follows a funeral until he prays over it then returns has a qirat; and whoever prays over it then walks with it until it is buried has two qirats. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the two qirats? He said: Like Uhud."
"13991","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili from Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' from Ja'far ibn Maysara al-Ashja'i from his father from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the procrastinating women. We said: O Prophet of Allah, what are the procrastinating women? He said: She whom her husband calls to his bed and she says: Later, until sleep overcomes him."
"13992","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili from Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' from Ja'far ibn Maysara from his father from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed one day among graves with a moist palm stalk, split it in two, placed one upon a grave and the other upon another grave, then went on. We said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you do that? He said: As for one of them, he was punished for talebearing, and as for the other, he did not guard against urine; and they will not be punished so long as this remains moist."
"13993","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili from Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' from Ja'far ibn Maysara from his father from Ibn Umar who said: The polytheists would not pour forth from Arafat until the sun turbaned the mountain tops, becoming upon their peaks like men's turbans upon their faces; while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pour forth until it set. And the polytheists would not pour forth from Muzdalifa (Jam') until they said: Let Thabir shine, and they would not pour forth until the sun was upon the mountain tops like men's turbans upon their faces; while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pour forth before the sun rose."
"13994","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il from Mindal ibn Ali from Ja'far ibn Abi Ja'far al-Ashja'i from his father from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led his Companions in Fajr prayer on a journey and recited: Say, O disbelievers and Say, He is Allah, the One; then he said: I have recited to you a third of the Qur'an and a quarter of it."
"13995","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili from Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' from Musa ibn Mutayr from his father from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes use the toothstick at night four times."
"13996","Narrated Musa ibn Harun and Abd al-Salam ibn Sahl al-Sukkari, both saying: Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ruzzi from Abu Tumayla Yahya ibn Wadih from Abu Tayba from Abu Mijlaz from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears silk and drinks from silver is not of us; and whoever alienates a wife against her husband or a slave against his masters is not of us."
"13997","Narrated Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi from Amr ibn Marzuq from Shu'ba from Qatada from Abu Mijlaz who said: I prayed behind Ibn Umar and he did not perform qunut, so I said: What prevented you from qunut? He said: I do not retain it from any of my companions."
"13998","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib from Abd Allah ibn Salih al-Ijli from Abthar ibn al-Qasim from Sulayman al-Taymi from Abu Mijlaz who said: Ibn Umar said: As for us, we used to give the fitr charity as dates."
"13999","Narrated Musa ibn Harun from Sa'id ibn Amr al-Ash'athi from Abthar ibn al-Qasim from Sulayman al-Taymi from Abu Mijlaz from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Zuhr prayer and prostrated, then stood and recited; and they thought he recited Alif Lam Mim, the revelation of al-Sajda."
"14000","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil from Ali ibn al-Ja'd from Shu'ba from Abu al-Tayyah who said: I heard Abu Mijlaz narrating from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Witr is one rak'a at the end of the night."
"14001","Narrated Durran ibn Sufyan ibn Mu'awiya al-Attar al-Basri from Muhammad ibn Kathir from Hammam from Qatada from Abu Mijlaz who said: I asked Ibn Umar about witr. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: One rak'a."
"14002","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Shu'ba from Qatada from Abu Mijlaz who said: I asked Ibn Umar about witr. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: One rak'a at the end of the night."
"14003","Narrated Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumanii from Salih al-Murri from Abu Harun from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When people pray together (in congregation), Allah indeed marvels at them."
"14004","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Hammad ibn Zayd from Abu Harun al-Abdi from Ibn Umar who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Peace be upon you. He said: Ten. Then another came and said: Peace be upon you and Allah's mercy. He said: Twenty. Then another came and said: Peace be upon you and Allah's mercy and His blessings. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Thirty."
"14005","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, both saying: Narrated Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi from Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi from his father from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution once each and said: This is the obligatory ablution without which Allah accepts no prayer; then he performed ablution twice each and said: This is the moderate (manner) of ablution, and Allah doubles the reward for its doer twofold; then he performed ablution three times each, then said: This is my ablution, and the ablution of Ibrahim, the intimate friend of Allah (peace be upon him), and the ablution of the prophets before me, Allah's blessings upon them; and whoever says after finishing: I testify that there is no god but Allah alone without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable — Allah opens for him eight gates of Paradise."
"14006","Narrated Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani and Musa ibn Harun, both saying: Narrated Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani from al-Furat ibn Abi al-Furat who said: I heard Mu'awiya ibn Qurra narrating from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed a man for a task, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me. He said: Keep to your house."
"14007","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Aban ibn Yazid from Anas ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar who said: I retained from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten rak'as: two before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Fajr."
"14008","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abu Asim from Ibn Awn from Anas ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about night prayer. He said: Two by two."
"14009","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Hammad ibn Salama from Anas ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Night prayer is two by two; when you fear dawn, pray odd with one rak'a."
"14010","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib ibn al-Shahid from his father from his grandfather Habib ibn al-Shahid from Anas ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night two by two."
"14011","Narrated Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti from Hilal ibn Bishr from Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Duba'i from al-Nahhas ibn Qahm from Anas ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar who said: I was between the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the man who asked him about night prayer, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Night prayer is two by two; when you fear dawn, pray odd with one rak'a."
"14012","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal from Salama ibn Alqama from Anas ibn Sirin who said: I asked Ibn Umar about witr. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Isha he would come to his bed, then rise in the night and pray two rak'as by two rak'as, until when it was the end of the night he prayed odd with one rak'a; then when morning came and dawn rose he prayed two rak'as, as though the call to prayer were in his ears (i.e. hastening)."
"14013","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim Abu al-Nu'man from Hammad ibn Zayd from Anas ibn Sirin who said: I said to Ibn Umar: Tell me about the two rak'as before the dawn prayer — shall I prolong recitation in them? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night two by two and pray odd with one rak'a. I said: That is not what I ask you about! He said: You are indeed bulky (slow to understand); will you not let me recite the narration to you in order?! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night two by two and pray odd with one rak'a, and pray two rak'as before the dawn prayer, as though the call to prayer were at his ears. Hammad said: Meaning quickly."
"14014","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from his father who said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting: Narrated Mustalim ibn Sa'id from Mansur ibn Zadham from Anas ibn Sirin from Abd Allah ibn Umar from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever buys or is gifted a ram, let him divide it into three portions, eating one portion each day on an empty stomach; if he wishes he melts it, and if he wishes he eats it — meaning the ram's fatty tail, used as remedy for sciatica. Abu al-Qasim said: He melts it, i.e. dissolves it."
"14015","Narrated Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinna'i from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab from Sufyan ibn Musa from Ayyub from Anas ibn Sirin who said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man with no wealth who buys on credit intending repayment. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every treacherous one there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection."
"14016","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, and narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Sulayman ibn Harb, both saying: Narrated Shu'ba from Anas ibn Sirin who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and Umar mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Let him take her back; when she is pure, let him divorce her. I said to him: Is it counted? He said: Bah (i.e. of course)!?"
"14017","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman from Abu Mu'awiya from Isma'il ibn Muslim from Muhammad and Anas, the sons of Sirin, that a man asked Ibn Umar about a man divorcing his wife while she menstruates. Ibn Umar said: Abd Allah ibn Umar did that, and Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Evil is what he did! Command him to take her back; when she is pure, let him divorce her if he wishes, and if he wishes let him keep her."
"14018","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Sahl ibn Uthman from Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman from Anas ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar that he divorced his wife while she menstruated, and Umar mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Command him to take her back; when she is pure, let him divorce her."
"14019","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Hisham ibn Hassan from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Night prayer is two by two, and witr is one rak'a at the end of the night. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Maghrib is the witr of the daytime; so make odd your night prayer."
"14020","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar from Ayyub from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Night prayer is two by two, and witr is one rak'a at the end of the night. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Maghrib is the witr of the daytime; so make odd your night prayer."
"14021","Narrated Ward ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti from Safwan ibn Salih from al-Walid ibn Muslim from Salim al-Khayyat from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Night prayer is two by two, and witr is one rak'a at the end of the night."
"14022","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Ibn Abi Adi from Yunus from Muhammad from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Night prayer is two by two; when you fear dawn, pray odd with one rak'a."
"14023","Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti from Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi from Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman who said: I heard Abu Shu'ayb narrating from Muhammad ibn Sirin, Anas ibn Sirin and Nafi' that they narrated to him from Ibn Umar who said: Ten prayers I retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): two rak'as before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Fajr."
"14024","Narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji from al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn from Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami from al-Hakam ibn Atiyya from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: I retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten rak'as: two before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Fajr."
"14025","Narrated al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi from Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq al-Razi from his father from Amr ibn Abi Qays from Asim al-Ahwal from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar who said: I retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): two rak'as before Zuhr, four after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Fajr."
"14026","Narrated Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-Askari from Ammar ibn al-Mukhtar from his father from Yunus ibn Ubayd from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar who said: I retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten rak'as: two before Zuhr, two after Zuhr, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Fajr."
"14027","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Nu'aym ibn Ya'qub and Yahya ibn Talha al-Yarbu'i, both saying: Narrated Fudayl ibn Iyad from Hisham ibn Hassan from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ashajj Abd al-Qays: In you are two traits Allah loves: forbearance and deliberation."
"14028","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Hisham ibn Ammar from Isma'il ibn Ayyash from Ibn Awn from Ibn Sirin who said: I asked Ibn Umar about sacrifices, are they obligatory? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed, and the Muslims after him, and the practice was established thereby."
"14029","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Murri from Ali ibn Salih from Umar ibn Rabi'a from al-Hasan from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about Paradise. He said: Whoever enters Paradise lives therein and does not die, enjoys therein and does not suffer; his garments do not wear out nor does his youth perish. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, of what is its building? He said: A brick of gold and a brick of silver; its mortar is pungent musk, its soil saffron, its pebbles pearl and ruby."
"14030","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Hammad ibn Salama from Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in what he relates from his Lord, blessed and exalted, who said: Whichever servant of Mine goes forth striving in My path seeking My pleasure, I guarantee him that if I return him, I return him with whatever reward or booty he attained, or if I take him I forgive him, have mercy on him and admit him to Paradise."
"14031","Narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi from Asim ibn Ali from his father Ali ibn Asim from Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant swallows a draught more excellent than a draught of anger he suppresses seeking Allah's countenance."
"14032","Narrated Abu Hanifa Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Ahwazi from Ma'mar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi from Ubayd Allah ibn Tammam from Yunus from al-Hasan from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever calls to guidance and is followed therein has the like of their rewards without diminishing anything from their rewards; and whoever calls to misguidance bears the like of their sins without diminishing anything from their sins."
"14033","Narrated Abu Hanifa Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti from Ma'mar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi from Ubayd Allah ibn Tammam from Yunus from al-Hasan from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man should let three (nights) pass him but that his will is written with him."
"14034","Narrated Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi from Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar al-Himsi from his father from Shu'ayb ibn Ruziq from Ata' al-Khurasani from al-Hasan from Abd Allah ibn Umar that he divorced his wife one divorce while she menstruated, then wished to follow it with two other divorces at the remaining two menstrual cycles; that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: O Ibn Umar, thus Allah did not command; you have erred from the practice. The practice is that you face a period of purity, divorcing at each cycle. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me and I took her back, then said: When she menstruates then becomes pure, divorce then or keep. I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me, had I divorced her thrice would I be able to take her back? He said: Then she would be separated from you, and it would be disobedience."
"14035","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Muhammad ibn Dinar from Yunus ibn Ubayd from Ziyad ibn Jubayr from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit."
"14036","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki from Hafs ibn Umar al-Juddi from Abd al-Warith from Ayyub from Ziyad ibn Jubayr who said: Ibn Umar saw a man slaughtering a sacrificial camel while it was kneeling, and said: Make it stand, for it is the practice of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14037","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal from Yazid ibn Zuray' from Yunus ibn Ubayd from Ziyad ibn Jubayr who said: I was with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: I vowed to fast every Tuesday or Wednesday as long as I live, and this day coincided with the Day of Sacrifice (Eid al-Adha). Ibn Umar said: Allah commanded fulfilling vows, and we were forbidden to fast this day."
"14038","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Minhal ibn Bahr from Ibn Awn from Ziyad ibn Jabir or Jabir ibn Ziyad — Ibn Awn doubted — that a woman came to Ibn Umar on a Thursday and said: I vowed to fast every Thursday, and that day coincided with Eid; shall I fast it? Ibn Umar said to her: Allah commanded us to fulfill vows, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from fasting this day."
"14039","Narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna al-Anbari from his father from his grandfather from Qurra ibn Khalid from Ma'ruf ibn Bashir from Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of al-dubba' and al-hantam (gourds and green jars)."
"14040","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Sahl ibn Bakkar from Aban ibn Yazid from Qatada from Abd Allah ibn Babi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the tashahhud: Greetings, good words, prayers belong to Allah; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and Allah's mercy and His blessings; peace upon us and upon Allah's righteous servants; I testify that there is no god but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."
"14041","Narrated Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Tayalisi from Nuh ibn Habib al-Qumasi from Azhar ibn al-Qasim from al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id from Qatada from Abd Allah ibn Babi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like thereof."
"14042","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i from Rawh ibn Ata' ibn Abi Maymuna from Ghaylan, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding wiping over the two socks: a day and night for the resident, and three days and their nights for the traveler."
"14043","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, and narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz from Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi, all saying: Narrated Hammam from Qatada from Abu al-Siddiq from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in their graves, say: In Allah's name and upon the practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14044","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Hisham al-Dastuwa'i from Qatada from Abu al-Siddiq that Ibn Umar, when the dead was placed in the grave, would say: In Allah's name and upon the practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14045","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz from Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi from Shu'ba from Qatada from Abu al-Siddiq from Ibn Umar who said: When you place the dead in his grave, say: In Allah's name and upon the practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14046","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Aban ibn Yazid from Qatada; and narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani from Hudba ibn Khalid from Hammam from Qatada; and narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad; and narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratiisi from al-Abbas ibn Talib, both saying: Narrated Abu Awana from Qatada; and narrated Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yazid ibn Zuray' from Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba and Hisham al-Dastuwa'i, from Qatada from Safwan ibn Muhriz al-Mazini who said: While I was walking with Ibn Umar, a man met him and said: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speak of the private converse (najwa)? He said: I heard him say: The believer draws near to his Lord, blessed and exalted, until He places His shelter over him, and it is said to him: Do you recognize such and such? He says: Yes. He says: I concealed them for you in the world, and I forgive them for you today. So he is given his scroll of good deeds. As for the disbeliever and the hypocrite, they are called out over the heads of witnesses: These are those who lied against their Lord; indeed Allah's curse is upon the wrongdoers. The wording is that of the narration of Muslim from Aban, the others similar."
"14047","Narrated Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi from Shu'ba from Qatada from Safwan ibn Muhriz who said: I asked Ibn Umar about prayer while traveling. He said: Two rak'as; whoever opposes the practice has disbelieved."
"14048","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Yazid ibn Ibrahim from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Yunus ibn Jubayr who said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she menstruated. He said: Do you know Abd Allah ibn Umar?! I said: Yes. He said: Abd Allah ibn Umar divorced his wife while she menstruated, and Umar ibn al-Khattab came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, so he commanded him to take her back then divorce her at the start of her waiting period. I said: Is it counted against her? He said: Yes. Tell me, if he is incapable and foolish?!"
"14049","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Sulayman ibn Harb from Hammad ibn Zayd from Ayyub and Salama ibn Alqama from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Ghallab Yunus ibn Jubayr who said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she menstruated. He said: Do you know Abd Allah ibn Umar?! He divorced his wife while she menstruated, and Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who commanded him to take her back. I said: Was it counted? He said: Bah?! Tell me, if he is incapable and foolish?!"
"14050","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar from Ayyub from Ibn Sirin who said: I spent twenty years hearing that Ibn Umar divorced his wife whom he divorced in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she menstruated, thrice, until Yunus ibn Jubayr informed me that he asked him: How many did you divorce your wife in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: One."
"14051","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from Asim from Ibn Sirin who said: Ibn Umar was asked: Did you count it — meaning the divorce with which he divorced her while she menstruated — and he said: What prevents them, if you were incapable and foolish?! Al-Thawri did not mention Yunus ibn Jubayr in his narration from Asim, while Amr ibn Abi Qays rendered it well."
"14052","Narrated al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi from Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq from his father from Amr ibn Abi Qays from Asim from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Yunus Abu Ghallab who said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man divorcing his wife while she menstruates. He said: Do you know Ibn Umar?! I said: Yes. He said: I divorced my wife while she menstruated, and Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Let him take her back until she is pure, then let him divorce her or keep her."
"14053","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim from Yunus ibn Ubayd from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Yunus ibn Jubayr who said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man divorcing his wife while she menstruates. He said: Do you know Abd Allah ibn Umar?! I said: Yes. He said: He divorced his wife while she menstruated, and Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take her back then divorce her, facing her waiting period."
"14054","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Hammam from Qatada from Abu Ghallab Yunus ibn Jubayr who said: I said to Ibn Umar: A man divorced his wife while she menstruated? He said: Do you know Ibn Umar?! Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she menstruated, and Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he commanded him to take her back; when she is pure, if he wishes to divorce her let him divorce her. I said: Was that counted as a divorce? He said: Tell me, if he is incapable and foolish?!"
"14055","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Hisham al-Dastuwa'i from Qatada from Yunus ibn Jubayr that a man asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she menstruated. He said: Do you know Ibn Umar?! He divorced his wife while she menstruated, and Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he said: Keep her with you; when she is pure, if he wishes he keeps, and if he wishes he divorces. I said: Is that divorce counted? He said: Bah?! Tell me, if he is incapable or foolish?!"
"14056","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Amr ibn Marzuq, and narrated Durran ibn Sufyan al-Attar al-Basri from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, and narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz, both saying: Narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi — all saying: Narrated Shu'ba from Qatada from Yunus ibn Jubayr that Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she menstruated, and Umar mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Command him to take her back; when she is pure, let him divorce her if he wishes. I said: Is it counted? He said: Bah, tell me, if he is incapable and foolish?!"
"14057","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Na'ila al-Asbahani from Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali from Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim from Qatada from Yunus ibn Jubayr who said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife one divorce while she menstruated. He said: Do you know Abd Allah ibn Umar?! I said: Yes. He said: He divorced his wife while she menstruated, and Umar ibn al-Khattab came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, and he commanded him to take her back until she is pure; if he wishes he keeps, and if he wishes he divorces."
"14058","Narrated Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari from Tahir ibn Khalid ibn Nizar from his father from Ibrahim ibn Tahman from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj from Qatada from Yunus ibn Jubayr who said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she menstruated. He said: He divorced his wife while she menstruated, and Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him take her back; when she is pure, let him divorce her if he wishes. I said to him: And it was a divorce? He said: Yes. Tell me, if Ibn Umar is incapable and foolish?!"
"14059","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Uqba ibn Mukram from Abd Allah ibn Isa al-Khazzaz from Yahya al-Bakka' from Ibn Umar that a Habashi (Ethiopian) was buried in Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He was buried in the clay from which he was created."
"14060","Narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji from Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi from Abd Allah ibn Isa from Yahya al-Bakka' that he heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever of you goes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"14061","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Nu'aym ibn Ya'qub from Abd al-Aziz al-Narmaqi from Yahya al-Bakka' from Ibn Umar who said: A man belched in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Keep your belching from us, for the most satiated of them in this world are the longest in hunger on the Day of Resurrection."
"14062","Narrated Habab ibn Salih al-Wasiti from Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasa'i from Ali ibn Asim from Yahya al-Bakka' from Ibn Umar who said: Duba'a bint al-Zubayr wished to perform Hajj, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Perform Hajj and say: My release (from ihram) is where You confine me."
"14063","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratiisi from Asad ibn Musa from Hammad ibn Salama from Yahya al-Bakka' who said: I said to Ibn Umar: We visit the rulers and praise them to their faces, but when we leave them we say otherwise? He said: We used to count this as hypocrisy in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14064","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil from Ali ibn al-Ja'd from Shu'ba from Qatada from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani and Bishr ibn al-Muhtafiz from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Silk is the garment of one who has no share (in the Hereafter)."
"14065","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Umar ibn al-Mughira from Ghalib al-Qattan from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani from Ibn Umar who said: We used to say of the killer of a believer, when he died, that he is in the Fire, and say of one who committed a major sin and died upon it, that he is in the Fire — until this verse was revealed: Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. So we did not declare them (doomed); we hoped for them and feared for them."
"14066","14029 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, [Surayj] ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi' and Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha, then slept a short sleep, then entered and circumambulated the House, meaning: at al-Muhassab."
"14067","14030 - Abu Shu'ayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ayyub and Hisham ibn Hassan and Ubayd Allah ibn Umar and Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, and from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Labbayk, O Allah, Labbayk; Labbayk, there is no partner for You, Labbayk; indeed praise, blessing and dominion belong to You; there is no partner for You."
"14068","14031 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he recited the Talbiyah, said: Labbayk, O Allah, Labbayk; Labbayk, there is no partner for You, Labbayk; indeed praise, blessing and dominion belong to You; there is no partner for You."
"14069","14032 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us; and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us; both said: Ubays ibn Maymun narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The parable of my Ummah is like the rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."
"14070","14033 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Benefit from this House, for it has been demolished twice, and it will be lifted away on the third time."
"14071","14034 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar who said: It is from the Sunnah to bathe when entering ihram and when entering Makkah."
"14072","14035 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Umar who said: Bathing on Friday is Sunnah."
"14073","14036 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn al-Walid al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jahdam, from Abd Allah ibn Badr, from Ibn Umar who said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not leave ihram, and with Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman, and they did not leave ihram."
"14074","14037 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muslim al-Qurri who said: I heard a man ask Ibn Umar, saying: Tell me, is Witr Sunnah? He said: Sunnah?! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Witr, as did the Muslims."
"14075","14038 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Duhaym [Abd al-Rahman] ibn Abbad ibn Isma'il al-Ma'wali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marwan al-Uqayli narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu al-Mu'adhdhal, that a man came to some people while they were praying, with Ibn Umar sitting behind them on something, and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what prevented you from praying? He said: I have already prayed, and we have been forbidden to pray twice in one day."
"14076","14039 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar al-Barra' narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', Abu Abd al-Salam narrated to me, saying: I said to Ibn Umar: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wear the turban? He said: He would wrap the coil of the turban around his head, tuck it in from behind, and let it hang down between his shoulders."
"14077","14040 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us; and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Suqayr narrated to us, my father Suqayr narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said - and my father had met him in Makkah - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day from his house with some of his Companions, and took one of the roads of Madinah, and passed by the courtyard of some people where a dead kid goat lay discarded in their courtyard. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over it and looked at it, then turned to his Companions and said: Do you see this kid goat, how worthless it became to its owners when they threw it away like this?! They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: By Allah, this world is more insignificant to Allah than this kid goat is to its owners."
"14078","14041 - Abu Shu'ayb Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, al-Nufayli narrated to us, Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Aqil ibn Talhah who said: I heard Abu al-Khasib say: I was sitting when Ibn Umar came, and a man stood up from his seat for him, but he refused to sit in it and sat in another place. The man kept saying to him: It would not have harmed you to do so. So he said: I would not sit in your seat, nor in anyone else's seat, after I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - a man came to him and another man stood up for him, intending to sit in his seat - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him."
"14079","14042 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Muhammad, the nephew of Sulaym ibn Hayyan al-Hudhali, narrated to us, my brother narrated to me, from my grandfather who said: We were with Ibn Umar when the Hajj of the people of Yemen and what they do in it was mentioned, and some of the people reviled them. So Ibn Umar said: Do not revile the people of Yemen, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The adornment of the pilgrims is the people of Yemen."
"14080","14043 - Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Utarid [Abu] al-Bazri, from Ibn Umar who said: We used to eat in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were walking, and we would drink while standing."
"14081","14044 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Khalid ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not strike the slave, for you do not know what you may coincide with."
"14082","14045 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, Ghassan ibn Burzin narrated to us, Rashid Abu Muhammad al-Himmani narrated to me, from Ibn Umar who said: We saw ourselves when none of us considered himself more entitled to his dinar and dirham than his Muslim brother; then the dinar and dirham became dearer to one of us than his Muslim brother. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When people are miserly with the dinar and dirham, and follow the tails of cattle, abandoning jihad, Allah will impose upon them a humiliation which He will not remove from them until they return to their affair."
"14083","14046 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Salim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mubashshir ibn Abi al-Malih, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no man over whom one hundred pray except that he is forgiven."
"14084","14047 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Ala' al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Mukhadish who said: I said to Ibn Umar: I performed Hajj and performed tamattu', but some of my companions disliked that? So Ibn Umar said: Allah has combined for you two rites; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that."
"14085","14048 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us, Abdan ibn Uthman narrated to us, from his father, from Shu'bah, from Mughirah ibn Mukhadish, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"14086","14049 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Simak al-Hanafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prayed one rak'ah with one group and one rak'ah with the other group in the fear prayer."
"14087","14050 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Simak al-Hanafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the House."
"14088","14051 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Mis'ar, from Simak al-Hanafi who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the House, or inside the Ka'bah."
"14089","14052 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Simak al-Hanafi who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in it, meaning: inside the House."
"14090","14053 - Ubayd al-Ijl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Thalj narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak al-Hanafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"14091","14054 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Simak al-Hanafi who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: It is not shortening, but rather it is complete; the two rak'ahs on a journey are Sunnah."
"14092","14055 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid al-Bunani who said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: I buy these walled gardens containing grapes, but I cannot sell them all as grapes until we press them? He said: Are you asking me about wine? I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We were sitting with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he raised his head toward the sky, then lowered it and scratched in the ground, and said: Woe to the Children of Israel!! Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, your statement about the Children of Israel has alarmed us. He said: There is no harm upon you from that; fat was forbidden to them, so they would melt it, then sell it, then eat its price; likewise the price of wine is unlawful for you."
"14093","14056 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani who said: I asked Ibn Umar, saying: A man moving pebbles in prayer? He said: Do not move the pebbles, for that is from Satan; rather do as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do: place your hand on your thigh, then say like this; and he placed his right palm on his right thigh and pointed with his forefinger."
"14094","14057 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani who said: I said to Ibn Umar: What do you say about the nabidh of the earthen jar - did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it? He said: They claim that. I said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: They claim that. Thabit said: So Allah turned him away from me; and when one of them was asked: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? he would become angry."
"14095","14058 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Thabit al-Bunani who said: I asked Ibn Umar about the nabidh of the earthen jar? He said: Unlawful. I said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it? So Ibn Umar said: They claim that."
"14096","14059 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Arabi who said: I heard a man ask Ibn Umar about touching the Black Stone? So Ibn Umar said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch it and kiss it. Then the man kept saying: What if I am crowded, what if I am overpowered? He said: Put your what-if in Yemen; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch it and kiss it."
"14097","14060 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Marthad ibn Amir al-Huna'i narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Nadbi, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, marvels at prayer in congregation."
"14098","14061 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the chamber of A'ishah saying: For every treacherous person there will be a banner on the Day of Resurrection according to the extent of his treachery."
"14099","14062 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, that Ibn Umar was asked about the lizard? He said: Since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about it what he said, we have refrained from eating it."
"14100","14063 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb who said: We said to Ibn Umar: How is the prayer of the traveler, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: If you follow the Sunnah of your Prophet I shall inform you; if you will not follow the Sunnah of your Prophet I shall not inform you. We said: The best of ways is the way of our Prophet, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left this Madinah, he did not add beyond two rak'ahs until he returned to it."
"14101","14064 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: You have been forbidden the hantam, you have been forbidden the naqir, you have been forbidden the muzaffat; all of these you have been forbidden."
"14102","14065 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: Do you see your standing when the imam finishes the surah - is this qunut?! By Allah, it is an innovation; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it for only a month, then abandoned it. Do you see your raising of hands in prayer?! And he raised his hand. By Allah, it is an innovation; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never did more than this at all, raising his hands up to his shoulders."
"14103","14066 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated in his qunut against Banu Usayyah, saying: O Allah, deal with Banu Usayyah, for they disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. He said: So fever was poured upon them."
"14104","14067 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the chamber of A'ishah: From here is the tribulation; and he pointed with his hand toward the east, and: From where the horn of Satan rises."
"14105","14068 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb who said: I asked Ibn Umar: May I take two dirhams for one dirham? He said: That is usury itself, so do not approach it. Have you not heard what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said?! He said: Take like for like."
"14106","14069 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Qasim, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was on the steps of the Ka'bah, saying: Praise be to Allah who fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the Confederates alone. Behold, every inherited honor from the Jahiliyyah is under my feet today, except the custodianship of the House and the providing of water to the pilgrims. Behold, bloodshed between deliberate and accidental - one killed with a whip or a stone - for it is one hundred camels, forty of them pregnant with their young."
"14107","14070 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Tawbah al-Anbari, from Mawraq al-Ijli who said: I said to Ibn Umar: Do you pray Duha? He said: No. I said: And Abu Bakr? He said: No. I said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I do not think so."
"14108","14071 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Hatim al-Allaf narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Mawraq al-Ijli and Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Umar who said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what I shall not abandon in residence nor on a journey: two rak'ahs before Zuhr and two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Fajr."
"14109","14072 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Mawraq al-Ijli who said: I asked Ibn Umar about prayer on a journey? He said: Two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs; whoever opposes the Sunnah has disbelieved."
"14110","14073 - Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, Mawraq al-Ijli narrated to us, saying: I asked Ibn Umar about the prayer of the traveler? He said: Two rak'ahs; whoever opposes the Sunnah has disbelieved."
"14111","14074 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hakkam narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Mawraq al-Ijli, from Ibn Umar who said: Safwan ibn Muhriz asked him about prayer on a journey? He said: Two rak'ahs; whoever opposes the Sunnah has disbelieved."
"14112","14075 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be thirty lying impostors."
"14113","14076 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn al-Taymi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr who said: al-Hawari ibn Ziyad narrated to me, saying: I was sitting with Abd Allah ibn Umar when a young man came to him and said: Will you not strive in jihad? He remained silent and turned away from him. Then Ibn Umar said: Islam is built upon four supports: establishing prayer and giving zakat, with no distinction between them, fasting the month of Ramadan, and Hajj to the House for whoever can find a way to it; and jihad and charity are among good deeds."
"14114","14077 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah and Nafi', that Ibn Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a verdict, saying: O Messenger of Allah, what if one of us becomes junub at night? He said: Let him perform ablution when he wishes to sleep."
"14115","14078 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn Umar who said: A man called out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which part of the night is most likely to have supplication answered? He said: The last depth of the night."
"14116","14079 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Yunus Abu Umayyah al-Saffar narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ayyub and Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."
"14117","14080 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith who said: When Ibn Umar went to his bed, he would say: O Allah, You created my soul and You take it; to You belong its life and its death. O Allah, if You take it, forgive it, and if You keep it alive, protect it. O Allah, I ask You for well-being. Then a man among his children said to him: O father, did Umar used to say this? He said: Rather one better than Umar used to say this."
"14118","14081 - Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Salih al-Harawi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Jamil ibn Zayd, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love your beloved moderately, for perhaps he will become hateful to you someday; and hate the one you hate moderately, for perhaps he will become beloved to you someday."
"14119","14082 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yunus al-Lu'lu'i narrated to us, Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Jamil ibn Zayd, from Ibn Umar who said: The prayer of travel is two rak'ahs; whoever opposes the Sunnah has disbelieved."
"14120","14083 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night prayer is two by two; then when you fear the dawn, prostrate a prostration."
"14121","14084 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night prayer is two by two; then when you fear the dawn, prostrate a single prostration, and two prostrations before the Fajr prayer."
"14122","14085 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same."
"14123","14086 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The night prayer? So he said with his finger like this: Two by two, and Witr is one rak'ah at the end of the night."
"14124","14087 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyub and Budayl al-Uqayli narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was between him and the questioner, saying: O Messenger of Allah, how is the night prayer? He said: Two by two; then when you fear the dawn, pray one rak'ah, and make the last of your prayer Witr."
"14125","14088 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ma'mar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The night prayer is two by two, giving salam after every two rak'ahs; then when you fear the dawn, pray Witr with one rak'ah."
"14126","14089 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Hasten the dawn with Witr."
"14127","14090 - Yusuf al-Qadi and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, both saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah who said: We were with Muhammad ibn Sirin, and with him was al-Mughirah ibn Salman, and he narrated, saying: Ibn Umar said: Ten rak'ahs I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): two before Zuhr, two after Zuhr, two after Maghrib, two after the last Isha, and two before Subh. Then a man with Muhammad said: Is this unavoidable?! So Muhammad said: What is unavoidable is the obligatory prayer."
"14128","14091 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Salman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: Ten rak'ahs I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): two before Zuhr, two after Zuhr, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Fajr."
"14129","14092 - Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn A'yan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from al-Mughirah ibn Salman, from Ibn Umar who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) four before Zuhr and two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Fajr."
"14130","14093 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from al-Mughirah ibn Salman, from Ibn Umar who said: Ten rak'ahs besides the obligatory I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): two before Zuhr and two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two before Subh."
"14131","14094 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Zayd, from Qaza'ah ibn Yahya who said: I was with Ibn Umar on a journey, and the caravan went ahead of his mount, and he began reciting and bowing and prostrating wherever he was facing. When morning came I said to him: I saw you do something you did not used to do? He said: I saw Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it."
"14132","14095 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Qaza'ah, that he asked Ibn Umar about prayer on the mount in whatever direction it faces - is it from the Sunnah? He said: Yes."
"14133","14096 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to me, Abu Tumaylah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muslim Abu Taybah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that a man of the Ansar had a son who would go out whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him about him, saying: Do you love him? He said: O Prophet of Allah, yes; then may Allah love you as I love him. So he said: Allah loves me more intensely than you love him. It was not long before that son of his died, and he went to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with grief apparent upon him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are you grieved? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Would you not be pleased that your son be with my son Ibrahim, playing with him under the shade of the Throne?! He said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah."
"14134","14097 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Awanah al-Shashi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, Marwan ibn al-Muqaffa' narrated to us, saying: I saw Ibn Umar grasp his beard and cut what exceeded the fist, and he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast, he would say: Thirst has gone, the veins are moistened, and the reward is confirmed, if Allah wills."
"14135","14098 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Maysur ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ubayd Allah ibn [Salim], from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill the snakes, for we have not made peace with them since we warred against them."
"14136","14099 - Bakr ibn Muhammad Abu Umar al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated to us, Umar ibn Abd Allah al-Rumi narrated to us, Awn al-Uqayli narrated to us, that Ibn Umar mentioned from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Gold for gold, weight for weight, and silver for silver, weight for weight; whoever adds and seeks addition has committed usury. By Allah, Ibn Umar did not lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14137","14100 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Tariq al-Wabishi narrated to us, Bashir ibn Maymun al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These hearts are vessels, and the best of them are the most retentive. When you ask Allah, ask Him while confident of being answered, for Allah does not answer the supplication of one who calls Him from a heedless, inattentive heart."
"14138","14101 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami, that he heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Walid narrate from Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided or traveled and night overtook him, he would say: O earth, my Lord and your Lord is Allah; I seek refuge in Allah from your evil, the evil within you, the evil created in you, and the evil crawling upon you; I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the lion, the black snake, the serpent and the scorpion, and from the inhabitant of the town, and from the parent and the offspring."
"14139","14102 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a funeral be followed when a wailing woman accompanies it."
"14140","14103 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, that Abu Anbasah narrated to him, saying: I performed Hajj and met Abd Allah ibn Umar, and asked him - while Ibn al-Zubayr had revolted and al-Hajjaj had come out against him with an army - saying: What do you think, O Abu Abd al-Rahman, about our Hajj, for we fear being prevented from reaching the House? So Ibn Umar said: Proceed to the House until you fulfill what is due upon you; if you are prevented from reaching it, do as we did with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): slaughter the sacrificial animal if you have one with you, release ihram, and return."
"14141","14104 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Umar ibn Amr al-Ahmusi narrated to us, from al-Mukhariq ibn Abi al-Mukhariq who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Basin is as wide as between Adan and Amman; cooler than snow, sweeter than honey, and more fragrant than musk; its cups are like the stars of the sky; whoever drinks a draught from it will never thirst thereafter. The first people to come to it will be the poor among the Emigrants. A speaker said: And who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Those with disheveled heads, pale faces, and soiled garments; the gates are not opened for them, nor do they marry the inaccessible women; those who give all that is due upon them and do not take what is due to them."
"14142","14105 - al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda' al-Antaki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Imran al-Hadrami, from Umar ibn Hujr, from Abd al-Karim ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The weak imam is accursed."
"14143","14106 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas ibn Ya'qub al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Salamah al-Azdi narrated to us, from Maslamah ibn Ali al-Khushani, from Umayr ibn Hani', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Surat al-Hadid was revealed on Tuesday, and Allah created iron on Tuesday, and the son of Adam killed his brother on Tuesday; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cupping on Tuesday."
"14144","14107 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us; and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us; both said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, accepts the repentance of the servant so long as he has not reached the death rattle."
"14145","14108 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn al-Harith, from Zayd ibn Artah, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that Ibn Umar saw a youth praying, having lengthened his prayer and drawn it out. He said: Who knows this one? A man said: I do. So Abd Allah ibn Umar said: Had I known him, I would have commanded him to lengthen the bowing and prostration, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When a servant stands to pray, his sins are brought and placed upon his head and shoulders; whenever he bows and prostrates, they fall away from him."
"14146","14109 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Munib al-Jurashi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent before the Hour with the sword, until Allah alone, with no partner, is worshipped; my provision was placed under the shade of my spear; humiliation and abasement were placed upon whoever opposes me; and whoever imitates a people is among them."
"14147","14110 - Musa ibn Sahl Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Abu al-Munib al-Jurashi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of the hadith of Ibn Thawban."
"14148","14111 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Afiyah ibn Ayyub narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to me, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu al-Zahiriyyah narrated to me, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the signs of affliction and the portents of the Hour: minds will depart, discernment will decrease, killing will increase, the signs of good will be lifted, and tribulations will appear."
"14149","14112 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Sinan, Abu al-Zahiriyyah narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has lifted the world before me, so I look at it and at what will occur in it until the Day of Resurrection, as if I were looking at this palm of mine - a clear unveiling from Allah, unveiled to His Prophet as it was unveiled to the prophets before him."
"14150","14113 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten the rows, for you line up as the angels line up; align the shoulders, close the gaps, be gentle in the hands of your brothers, and do not leave gaps for the devils. Whoever joins a row, Allah joins him; and whoever cuts a row, Allah cuts him."
"14151","14114 - Muhammad ibn Sufyan ibn Jarir al-Ramli narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wearing the upper garment is the dress of the Arabs, and wrapping oneself is the dress of faith; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wrap himself."
"14152","14115 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Sinan, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Abu Shajarah, from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in Witr: {Glorify the name of your Lord}, and: {Say, O disbelievers}, and: {Say, He is Allah, the One}."
"14153","14116 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Sinan, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Abu Shajarah, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Establishing one of the prescribed punishments of Allah is better than forty nights of rain falling in the lands of Allah."
"14154","14117 - Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Ulayy narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever greets twenty men of the Muslims in a day, together or individually, then dies on that day of his, Paradise becomes due for him; and likewise in his night."
"14155","14118 - Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Afiyah ibn Ayyub narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to me, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Ummah after me will surely be tested with tribulations like the dark portions of the night; a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning; some people will sell their religion for a small portion of this world."
"14156","14119 - al-Fadl ibn Harun al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abd Allah al-Kala'i, from Abu Abd Allah al-Qurashi, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Yellowness is the dye of the believer, redness is the dye of the Muslim, and black is the dye of the disbeliever."
"14157","14120 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lah'iah informed us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Ibn Hujayrah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four things, if they are in you, then whatever you miss of this world will not harm you: guarding the trust, truthful speech, good character, and chastity in food."
"14158","14121 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lah'iah informed us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Ibn Hujayrah al-Akbar, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except over two: a man to whom Allah has given the Qur'an, so he recites it by night and day; and a man to whom Allah has given wealth, so he spends it in the path of Allah or in obedience to Allah."
"14159","14122 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um narrated to us, from Abu Ghutayf who said: I was with Ibn Umar, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs ablution while already in a state of purity, Allah writes for him ten good deeds."
"14160","14123 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um informed me, from Yazid ibn Qasit al-Saksaki who said: I asked Ibn Umar about fasting on a journey? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast on a journey and break his fast; and I fast and break my fast."
"14161","14124 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Lah'iah narrated to us, Abu Tu'mah narrated to me, saying: I was with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I am strong enough to fast on a journey? So Ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever does not accept the concession of Allah, upon him will be sin like the mountains of Arafah."
"14162","14125 - Mas'ud ibn Muhammad al-Ramli Abu al-Jarud narrated to us, Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us, Ibn Lah'iah narrated to us, Abu Tu'mah narrated to me, that he heard Ibn Umar say: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I heard him say: Allah has cursed wine, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its drinker, its server, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, and the eater of its price."
"14163","14126 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf and Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Yazid informed us, Abu Hani' narrated to me, from Abbas al-Hajari, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: How often should we pardon our slaves? He said: Pardon them seventy times every day."
"14164","14127 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Abu Hani' al-Khawlani narrated to me, from Abbas ibn Julayd al-Hajari, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that he heard him say: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, how often should we pardon the servant? He remained silent; then he repeated the words to him and he remained silent; then on the third time he said: Pardon him seventy times every day."
"14165","14128 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from Uqbah ibn Muslim who said: I asked Abd Allah ibn Umar about Witr? He said: While we were in the mosque, a man stood and asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Witr and about the night prayer? He said: The night prayer is two by two; then when morning comes upon you and you fear the dawn, pray Witr with one."
"14166","14129 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Lah'iah narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, that Abd Allah ibn Rafi' al-Hadrami narrated to him, that he heard Abd Allah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would begin with the prayer on al-Fitr and al-Adha."
"14167","14130 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Lah'iah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Sharahil ibn Bukayl al-Khawlani, from his father, that he asked Abd Allah ibn Umar about juice? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah destroy the Jews; fat was forbidden to them, yet they sold it and ate its price."
"14168","14131 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Rabi'ah ibn Sayf who said: We were with Shufayy al-Asbahi who said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: O Uthman, if Allah clothes you with a shirt and the people want you to take it off, do not take it off; for by Allah, if you take it off, you will not see Paradise until the camel passes through the eye of the needle."
"14169","[continuation, via key 14168: Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi from Abd Allah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Khalid ibn Yazid from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal from Rabi'ah ibn Sayf, from Abd Allah ibn Umar] I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be after me twelve caliphs: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who will not remain after me except briefly; and the master of the millstone of the Arabs' abode, who will live praiseworthily and be killed as a martyr. Then a man said: Who is he, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"14170","14132 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Muhammad ibn al-Nil al-Fihri narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while the people were performing voluntary prayers after the rising of Fajr, and said: There is no prayer after the rising of Fajr except two rak'ahs."
"14171","14133 - Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Nil narrated to me, that Abu Bakr ibn Yazid ibn Sarjis narrated to him, that Abd Allah ibn Umar saw a freed slave of his - called Yasar - praying after the rising of Fajr. He said: What is this prayer? He said: Something remaining upon me from my portion. So Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us after the Fajr prayer and said: When Fajr rises, there is no prayer except two rak'ahs; let the witness convey to the absent."
"14172","14134 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir al-Yamami narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Badr, from Ibn Umar who said: The Qur'an was revealed with wiping, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to wash, and we washed."
"14173","14135 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Bazi' Abu Umar, freed slave of Banu Makhzum, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two kinds of dress: the notorious for its fineness, and the notorious for its ugliness."
"14174","14136 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Marwan narrated to us, Furat ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade backbiting and listening to backbiting."
"14175","14137 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Marwan narrated to us, Furat ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade tale-bearing and listening to tale-bearing."
"14176","14138 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Marwan narrated to us, Furat ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade relieving oneself on the bank of a flowing river."
"14177","14139 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, Furat ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to send a man on an errand that concerned him, with Abu Bakr on his right and Umar on his left. So Ali said to him: What prevents you from these two? He said: How can I send these two when they are to the religion like hearing and sight are to the head?!"
"14178","14140 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqall al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, saying: I read to Ma'qil ibn Ubayd Allah, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Magians, saying: They let their mustaches grow long and shave their beards. And Ibn Umar would inspect his mustache and trim it as a sheep is shorn."
"14179","14141 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Sinan, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has his property sought and fights, then is killed, is a martyr."
"14180","14142 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Isa ibn Salim al-Shashi narrated to us, Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he commanded him to take her back and not touch her until she becomes pure; then when she becomes pure, if he wishes he may divorce, and if he wishes he may keep."
"14181","14143 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Abu al-Malih narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran who said: A man asked Ibn Umar about the statement of Allah, mighty and majestic: {And fight them until there is no fitnah}? He said: We fought with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until there was no fitnah; so go, you and your companions, and fight until there is fitnah."
"14182","14144 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Baylamani narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no preemption for an absent one nor a minor, nor for a partner against a partner when preceded by purchase; and preemption is like the untying of the hobble."
"14183","14145 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Uthaym say: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Baylamani narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What is permissible among witnesses in fosterage? He said: A man and his wife."
"14184","14146 - al-Abbas ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tha'lab narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn al-Abbas, from Ibn al-Baylamani, from his father, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Debt is of two kinds: whoever dies intending to repay it, I am his guardian; and whoever dies not intending to repay it, that is the one whose good deeds will be taken - there will be no dinar nor dirham on that day."
"14185","14147 - al-Abbas ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tha'lab narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn al-Abbas, from Ibn al-Baylamani, from his father, from Ibn Umar who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed by which Allah will benefit me. He said: Upon you are the two rak'ahs of Fajr, for in them is excellence."
"14186","14148 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Uthman ibn Yazdawayh, from Ya'fur ibn Rudhi who said: I heard Ubayd ibn Umayr narrating, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the hypocrite is like a sheep lying between two flocks. So Ibn Umar said: Woe to you! Do not lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the hypocrite is like a bleating sheep between two flocks."
"14187","14149 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Bahir informed us, saying: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid al-San'ani say: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at the Day of Resurrection as if with the sight of the eye, let him recite: {When the sun is folded up}, and: {When the sky is rent asunder}, and: {When the sky is cleft}; and I think he mentioned Surat Hud."
"14188","Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, kunya Abu Muhammad - mention of his age, death, and reports about him. 14150 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri mentioned to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, kunya Abu Muhammad, died in Egypt, and was buried in his small house, in the year sixty-five; and one saying: in the year sixty-eight. And his age was seventy-two years, or ninety-two years; Yahya ibn Bukayr doubted between seventy and ninety."
"14189","14151 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Amr died in the year sixty-five."
"14190","14152 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hani' Abu Hani' informed me, that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli say: Three men came to Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As while I was with him, and they said: O Abu Muhammad."
"14191","14153 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The Ka'bah was created two thousand years before the earth, and the earth was spread out from beneath it."
"14192","14154 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, from al-A'mash, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The House was placed two thousand years before the earth; and the House was a white foam when the Throne was upon the water, and the earth beneath it was like a dried date, then it was spread out from it."
"14193","14155 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father informed us, Mu'awiyah informed us, from al-A'mash, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, the like of it; saying: And the House was a foam."
"14194","14156 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The Sanctuary was placed two thousand years before the earth, and the earth was spread out from beneath it. Mujahid said: And His statement: {So make the hearts of people incline toward them} - he said: Had He said: the hearts of the people, Persia and Rome would have crowded upon it."
"14195","14157 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: When Allah sent Adam down from Paradise, He said: I am sending down with you a House, or an abode, around which circumambulation is performed as circumambulation is performed around My Throne, and at which prayer is performed as prayer is performed around My Throne. Then when the time of the Flood came, it was lifted; and the prophets would perform Hajj to it without knowing its place. Then He showed it to Ibrahim, so he built it from five mountains: from Hira', Thabir, Lubnan, Mount Tur, and Mount al-Habr; so benefit from it as much as you can."
"14196","14158 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, al-Nahhas ibn Qahm informed us, from Isl ibn Sufyan al-Yarbu'i, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: When Allah sent Adam down, He sent him down in the land of India, with cuttings from the trees of Paradise; so he planted them there. His head was in the sky and his feet on the earth, and he would hear the speech of the angels, which lightened his loneliness. Then he was pressed with a pressing, so he shrank to seventy cubits. Then Allah revealed: I am sending down upon you a House around which circumambulation is performed as the angels circumambulate around My Throne, and at which prayer is performed as the angels pray around My Throne. So he set out toward the House; every footstep became a village, and between his feet was wilderness, until he reached Makkah. He entered through the gate of al-Safa, circumambulated the House and prayed at it, then went out to Syria and died there."
"14197","14159 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Waki' informed us, from Sawadah ibn Abi al-Aswad, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: Circumambulate this House and touch this Stone, for they were two stones sent down from Paradise; one of them was lifted, and the other will be lifted. If it is not as I said, then whoever passes by my grave, let him say: This is the grave of Abd Allah ibn Amr the liar."
"14198","14160 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn al-Musayyab, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: Jibril, peace be upon him, brought this Stone down from Paradise; so benefit from it as much as you can, for you will remain in good so long as it remains among you; for it is imminent that he will come and return with it from where he brought it."
"14199","14161 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Dirar ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl who said: Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As said: Had I seen a man drinking wine with none seeing me but Allah, and I were able to kill him, I would kill him."
"14200","14162 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Ibn Lah'iah narrated to us, from Darraj who said: I saw Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As riding a mount before the funeral, until he reached the graveyard; then he dismounted and sat before the funeral arrived."
"14201","14163 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu Ma'mar Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar narrated to us, from his father, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: A quarter of those who do not wear clothes among the black people are more numerous than all people."
"14202","14164 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from al-Uryan ibn al-Haytham, from his father al-Haytham who said: I entered upon Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah, and while we were sitting with him, a man came to him and took hold of his elbows and leaned upon them. We said: Who is this? Some said: This is Abd Allah ibn Amr; and some of us said: O Abd Allah, we narrate hadiths from you. He said: You, company of the people of Iraq, take hadiths from their lower ends and do not take them from their upper ends. And they mentioned the Dajjal, so he said: Is there in your land a land called Kuktha, with salt marshes and palm trees? They said: Yes. He said: He will emerge from it."
"14203","14165 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Umar informed us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Ibrahim ibn Ubayd, freed slave of Abu Rifa'ah al-Zuraqi, from Abd Allah ibn Babayh who said: I came to Abd Allah ibn Amr at Arafah, and saw him having pitched a tent in the hilly area and a tent in the Sanctuary. I said to him: Why did you do this?! He said: My prayer will be in the Sanctuary, and when I go out to my family I shall be in the hilly area. I said to him: How do you pray Witr? He said: The Witr most pleasing to me is seven; Allah created seven heavens, seven earths, and seven days; tawaf around the House was made seven, between al-Safa and al-Marwah seven, and stoning the Jamarat seven pebbles. Then he said: Allah did not create anything on earth from Paradise except this ruby - the Black Corner; and by Allah it shall surely be lifted before the Day of Resurrection."
"14204","14166 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam informed us, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that a slave boy of his sold surplus water from an uncle of his for twenty thousand. So Abd Allah said: Do not sell it, for it is not lawful to sell it."
"14205","14167 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus informed me, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: Paradise is folded up, suspended upon the horns of the sun; it spreads out once every year. And the souls of the believers are in birds like starlings, recognizing one another therein, sustained from the fruits of Paradise. Khalid ibn Ma'dan said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, they will say: Our Lord, did You not promise us that You would bring us to the Fire?! He will say: Yes indeed, but you passed by it while it was extinguished."
"14206","14168 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Kathir ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Iyad, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The Throne is surely encircled by a serpent, and revelation indeed descends in chains."
"14207","14169 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid; and Abd Allah ibn Sulayman, from Amr ibn Nafi', from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that he passed by a man after the Subh prayer while he was sleeping. He moved him with his foot until he awoke, and said to him: Do you not know that Allah looks upon His creation at this hour, and admits a company of them into Paradise by His mercy."
"14208","14170 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: I read to Abu Qurrah, from Zam'ah ibn Salih, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The Black Corner descended from heaven, and was placed upon Abu Qubays like a white crystal; it remained forty years, then was placed upon the foundations of Ibrahim."
"14209","14171 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The people of the Fire will call Malik, but he will not answer them for forty years; then he will say: {Indeed you shall remain}. Then they will call their Lord, saying: {Our Lord, take us out of it; if we return, we are wrongdoers}. Then He will not answer them for the like of this world; then He will say: {Remain despised therein and do not speak to Me}. Then the people will despair; there will be nothing but bellowing and gasping, their voices resembling the voices of donkeys - its beginning a gasp and its end a bellow."
"14210","14172 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Shibl narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Muslim al-Hajari who said: I said to Abd Allah ibn Amr: O Abu Muhammad, from what was creation created? He said: From water and wind, from light and darkness. Then I went to Ibn Abbas and asked him about that? So he said therein as Abd Allah ibn Amr had said."
"14211","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq from his father from Jarir ibn Hazim from Mughira from Fudayl ibn Amr from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I find in the revealed Book of Allah: ""Whoever drinks wine and does not become intoxicated, his prayer will not be accepted for seven (days); if he dies during them he dies as a disbeliever; and if he drinks wine and becomes intoxicated, his prayer will not be accepted for forty mornings; if he dies during them he dies as a disbeliever."""
"14212","Narrated Muhammad from his father from Abu Amir al-Aqadi from Hisham ibn Sad from Zayd ibn Aslam from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani from Abdullah ibn Amr: When the servant is killed in the path of Allah, with the first drop of his blood that falls upon the earth Allah forgives him all his sins; then a cloth from Paradise is sent to him in which his soul is taken, and he is given a body from Paradise in which his spirit is placed; then he ascends with the angels as though he had been with them since Allah created him, until he is brought to heaven, and he passes no gate but it is opened for him, and no angel but he invokes blessings upon him and seeks forgiveness for him, until he is brought to al-Rahman, mighty and majestic, and he prostrates before the angels, then the angels prostrate after him; then he is forgiven and purified, then he is commanded to join the martyrs, and he finds them in green meadows and garments of silk, with them a bull and a whale that feed them each day with something different from the day before; the whale stays in the rivers of Paradise eating from every fragrance of the rivers of Paradise, and in the evening the bull gores it with its horn and slaughters it, and they eat from its flesh and find in its flesh every fragrance of the rivers of Paradise; and the bull spends the night grazing in Paradise eating from the fruits of Paradise, and in the morning the whale comes to it and slaughters it with its tail, and they eat from its flesh and find in the taste of its flesh the taste of every fruit in Paradise; they look at their dwellings and call upon Allah for the Hour to come. And when Allah takes the soul of the believing servant, He sends to him two angels with a cloth from Paradise and sweet basil from the basil of Paradise, and they say: O tranquil soul, come out to rest and basil, and to a Lord who is not angry; come out, for excellent is what you sent forth; and it comes out like the sweetest scent of musk any of you ever smelled with his nose, and upon the regions of the sky are angels saying: Glory be to Allah! Today there has come from the earth a pleasant spirit and a pleasant soul; and he passes no gate but it is opened for him, and no angel but he invokes blessings upon him and intercedes for him, until he is brought to al-Rahman, mighty and majestic, and the angels prostrate before him, then they say: Our Lord, this is Your servant so-and-so whose soul we took, and You know best about him; and He says: Command him to prostrate; and the soul prostrates, then Mika'il is called and it is said: Place this soul with the souls of the believers until I ask you about them on the Day of Resurrection. Then his body is commanded and it is widened for him, seventy in length and seventy in width, and basil is scattered in it and silk is spread in it and he is covered with silk; and if he had anything of the Quran with him its light clothes him, otherwise Allah makes for him a light like the light of the sun; then a door to Paradise is opened for him, and he looks at his seat in Paradise morning and evening. And when Allah takes the soul of the disbelieving servant, He sends to him two angels, and sends to him a piece of coarse hair-cloth more foul-smelling than every stench and rougher than every roughness, and they say: O wicked soul, come out to Hell and a painful punishment, and to a Lord angry against you; come out, for evil is what you sent forth; and it comes out like the foulest corpse any of you ever smelled with his nose, and upon the regions of the sky are angels saying: Glory be to Allah! Today there has come from the earth the smell of a corpse and a wicked soul; and the gate of heaven is not opened for him; and his body is commanded and it is tightened upon him in the grave, and it is filled with snakes like the necks of Bactrian camels eating his flesh, leaving nothing of his bones; then deaf and blind angels are sent against him, with them are iron mallets; they do not see him to have mercy on him, nor hear his voice to have mercy on him; and they strike him and beat him, and a door from the Fire is opened for him, and he looks at his seat in the Fire morning and evening, asking Allah to keep that upon him and not to bring him to what lies beyond it of the Fire."
"14213","What Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with him). Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father from Marwan ibn Shuja from Ibrahim ibn Abi Abla al-Uqayli of the people of Bayt al-Maqdis from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: Abdullah ibn Umar and Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As met at al-Marwa and conversed, then Abdullah ibn Amr went on and Abdullah ibn Umar remained weeping; a man said to him: What makes you weep, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: This one, meaning Abdullah ibn Amr, claimed that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride, Allah will cast him upon his face into the Fire."""
"14214","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from his father from Yala ibn Ubayd; and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr from Jafar ibn Awn, both from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi from his father from Abdullah ibn Umar from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""No person in whose heart is the weight of a mustard seed of pride will enter Paradise."""
"14215","Narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri from Said ibn Abi Maryam from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umama from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a dome had been pitched for him at the rear of the mosque, and two men were disputing, and I heard something shaking the ropes of the dome, and I turned and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looking out with his head uncovered, his face red, and he said: ""The nations before you were not destroyed until they fell into the like of this, striking parts of the Quran against others?! Whatever is lawful, declare it lawful, and whatever is unlawful, declare it unlawful, and whatever is ambiguous, believe in it."""
"14216","Sufyan ibn Awf from Abdullah. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Anas ibn Malik from Abdullah ibn Amr; and narrated Bishr ibn Musa from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri from Ibn Lahi'a; and narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri from Said ibn Abi Maryam from Abdullah ibn Lahi'a from al-Harith ibn Yazid from Jundub ibn Abdullah al-Adwani that he heard Sufyan ibn Awf al-Qari, a man of al-Qara, say: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the sun rose, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah will bring on the Day of Resurrection a people whose light is like the light of the sun""; Abu Bakr said: Are we they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""No, and for you is much good, but they are the poor emigrants who will be gathered from the regions of the earth""; then he said: ""Blessedness for the strangers, blessedness for the strangers""; it was said: Who are the strangers? He said: ""Righteous people, few among many evil people; those who disobey them are more than those who obey them."""
"14217","Narrated Ahmad ibn Rishdin from his father from his father from his grandfather from Amr ibn al-Harith from Abd al-Karim ibn al-Harith from his father al-Harith ibn Yazid that Jundub ibn Abdullah al-Adwani narrated to him that Sufyan ibn Awf al-Qari informed him that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day and the sun rose, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah will surely bring on the Day of Resurrection peoples whose light is like the light of the sun""; Abu Bakr and Umar said: Are we they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""You are not they, and for you is much good, but they are the poor emigrants who will be raised from the regions of the earth."""
"14218","Narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi from Arim from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad from Uthman ibn Hakim from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""The Hour will not come until people mount one another in the roads as beasts mount one another."""
"14219","Narrated Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Qattan al-Hamadhani Mammus from Muhammad ibn Sahm al-Antaki from Baqiyya; and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Atiyya ibn Baqiyya ibn al-Walid from his father from al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman from Ibn Jurayj from al-Zuhri from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the juma (large bun of hair) for the free woman and the aqisa (braided lock) for the slave girl."
"14220","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abda al-Massisi from Abu Tawba al-Rabi ibn Nafi from Isa ibn Yunus from Fitr ibn Khalifa from Abu al-Tufayl from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Kinship is a branch attached to the Throne; and the one who maintains ties is not the one who reciprocates, but the one who maintains ties is the one who joins his kinship when it is cut."""
"14221","Narrated Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab from Ali ibn al-Madini from Husayn al-Jufi from Za'ida from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib from Harb ibn Ubaydullah from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid who said: I retained from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to recite the Quran in five (days)."
"14222","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abdullah ibn Raja from Imran al-Qattan from Qatada from Said ibn al-Musayyib from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at a woman who is not grateful to her husband and cannot do without him."""
"14223","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak from Shu'ba from Qatada from Said ibn al-Musayyib from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like thereof."
"14224","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Shayban ibn Farrukh from Yazid ibn Iyad from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al-Musayyib from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to the people while they were praying and said: ""The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."""
"14225","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani from Ishaq ibn Zayd al-Khattabi from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud from his father from Abd al-Karim from Said ibn al-Musayyib who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr narrating one day to a gathering of Muslims among whom was Ibn Umar; he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever shows off his deed to people, Allah will expose him before the hearing of His creation and belittle him and make him small""; and I saw the eyes of Ibn Umar shedding tears."
"14226","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Yusuf al-Qadi who said: Narrated Musaddad; and narrated Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari from Zakariyya ibn Adi; and narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba from Yahya ibn Ma'in who said: Narrated Mutamir ibn Sulayman from his father from al-Hadrami from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Abdullah ibn Amr that a woman called Umm Mahzul, who used to stay at Ajyad and commit fornication, used to stipulate for a man if he married her that she would suffice him maintenance; and a man sought permission regarding her from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse, or he said: Then was revealed: ""And none marries the adulteress but an adulterer or a polytheist"" to the end of the verse; and the wording is that of Yahya ibn Ma'in."
"14227","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talha from his uncle from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever's wealth is sought unjustly and he fights and is killed, he is a martyr."""
"14228","Narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi from Qabisa; and narrated Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Massisi from Abu Hudhayfa; and narrated Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna who said: Narrated Muhammad ibn Kathir who said: Narrated Sufyan from Sad ibn Ibrahim from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Among the major sins is that a man reviles his parents""; they said: O Messenger of Allah, how can a man revile his parents? He said: ""A man reviles the father of (another) man, so he reviles his father; and he reviles his mother, so he reviles his mother."""
"14229","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Amr ibn Marzuq from Shu'ba from Sad ibn Ibrahim from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Among the gravest sin in Islam is that a man curses his parents""; it was said: O Messenger of Allah, how can a man curse his parents?! He said: ""A man trades insults with (another) man, so he curses his father and he curses his father, and he curses his mother and he curses his mother."""
"14230","Narrated Said ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira al-Misri from Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti from Ibrahim ibn Sad from his father from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Among the greatest of major sins is that a man curses his father""; they said: O Messenger of Allah, how can a man curse his father?! He said: ""He reviles the father of (another) man, so he reviles his father; and he reviles the mother of (another) man, so he reviles his mother."""
"14231","Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi from Abdullah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Ibn al-Had; and narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from Nuaym ibn Hammad al-Marwazi from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad from Yazid ibn al-Had from Sad ibn Ibrahim from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Among the greatest of major sins is a man's reviling his parents""; they said: O Messenger of Allah, can a man revile his parents?! He said: ""Yes; he reviles the father of (another) man, so he reviles his father; and he reviles his mother, so he reviles his mother."""
"14232","Narrated Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar from Yazid ibn Harun from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqama from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered my house and said: ""O Abdullah ibn Amr, have I not been informed that you burden yourself with standing in prayer at night and fasting in the day?"" I said: Indeed I do so; and he said: ""It suffices you to fast three days of every month, a good deed for ten like it, as though you fasted the whole year""; and I insisted and he was strict with me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I find strength for more than that; and he said: ""It suffices you, and do not say 'I will do,' to fast three days of every Friday (week)""; and I insisted and he was strict with me, and I said: I find strength for more than that. And he said: ""The most just fasting with Allah is the fast of Dawud; he used to fast half the year; your eyes have a right upon you, and your guest has a right upon you, and your family has a right upon you."" And Abdullah said, when old age reached him and he grew weak and old: That I had accepted the concession of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is dearer to me than my family and my wealth."
"14233","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban from Abu Salama from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Recite the Quran in a month""; he said: I find strength; he said: ""Recite in twenty""; he said: I find strength; he said: ""Recite in fifteen""; he said: I find strength; he said: ""Recite in ten""; he said: I find strength; he said: ""Recite in seven and do not add to that at all."""
"14234","Narrated Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi from al-Awzai from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salama from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Have I not been informed that you fast the day and stand in prayer at night?"" I said: Yes; he said: ""Do not do so; fast and break fast, stand and sleep; for your soul has a right upon you, and your body has a right upon you, and your wife has a right upon you, and your visitors have a right upon you; and it suffices you to fast three days of every month, for a good deed is for ten like it""; and I was strict and it was made strict upon me; I said: I find strength; he said: ""Then fast three days of every Friday (week)""; and I was strict and it was made strict upon me; I said: I find strength; he said: ""Then fast the fast of Dawud, Prophet of Allah, and do not add to it""; I said: And what is the fast of Dawud? He said: ""Half the year."" And Abdullah ibn Amr after he grew old used to say: Would that I had accepted the concession of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)!"
"14235","Narrated Ahmad ibn Masud al-Maqdisi from Muhammad ibn Kathir; and narrated Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani from Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti from al-Awzai from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Abdullah, do not be like so-and-so, for he used to stand in prayer at night then abandoned standing at night."""
"14236","Narrated Ahmad ibn Masud al-Maqdisi from Muhammad ibn Kathir from al-Awzai from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salama from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man will commit sacrilege in Makka called Abdullah, upon him is half the punishment of the world."""
"14237","Narrated Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti from Abu Nuaym from Shayban from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salama from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The sun eclipsed, and it was announced: Prayer in congregation! And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed two rak'as in the mosque, then sat until the sun cleared."
"14238","Narrated Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Tayalisi from Yahya ibn Ma'in from Wahb ibn Jarir from his father from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from al-Zuhri from Abu Salama from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."""
"14239","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i from Asad ibn Musa from Ibn Abi Dhi'b from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The curse of Allah is upon the briber and the bribe-taker."""
"14240","Narrated Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub al-Ahwazi from Ali ibn Bahr from Hisham ibn Yusuf from Ibn Jurayj from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah has cursed the briber and the bribe-taker."""
"14241","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Abu Salama from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Fasting three days of every month is the fasting of the whole year."""
"14242","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri from Khalid ibn Nizar from Isa ibn al-Muttalib from Ibn Shihab from Ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: I said: I shall fast the whole year as long as I live and stand in prayer at night as long as I live; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Are you the one who said: I shall fast the whole year as long as I live and stand at night as long as I live?"" I said: I did say that, O Messenger of Allah; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fast and break fast, pray and sleep, and fast three days of the month, and every good deed is for ten like it."" I said: I find in myself strength for better than that; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then fast a day and break fast two days."" I said: I find in myself strength for better than that; and he said: ""Then fast a day and break fast a day, for that is the fast of Dawud."" I said: I have strength for better than that; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is nothing better than that."""
"14243","Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi from Abdullah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salama from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed that I say: I shall fast the whole year and stand at night as long as I live; and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Isa ibn al-Muttalib."
"14244","Narrated Ali ibn Said from Ali ibn Muslim ibn al-Haytham al-Mu'addib from Yahya ibn Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi from his father from Bakr ibn Wa'il from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salama from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like thereof."
"14245","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from Abu Thabit Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Madini from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim from Yazid ibn al-Had from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Abu Salama from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: ""You fast the day and do not break fast, and you pray the night and do not sleep; it suffices you to fast three days of every month""; I said: O Messenger of Allah, I find in me a strength greater than that. He said: ""Then it suffices you to fast two days of every Friday (week)""; I said: O Messenger of Allah, until it reached the fast of Dawud: he used to fast a day and break fast a day."
"14246","Narrated Abu Shuayb al-Harrani from Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti from al-Awzai from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr who said: I asked Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, saying: Inform me of the harshest thing you saw the polytheists do to the Messenger of Allah; he said: Uqba ibn Abi Muayt came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying by the Ka'ba, and he twisted his garment around his neck and throttled him severely; and Abu Bakr came and took him by the shoulder and pushed him away from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Abu Bakr said: O people: ""Do you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah, when he has come to you with clear proofs"" to the end of the whole verse."
"14247","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, author of al-Maghazi, from Ibrahim ibn Sad from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Yahya ibn Urwa ibn al-Zubayr from his father Urwa from Abdullah ibn Amr that he said: How often did you see Quraysh harm the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what they showed of enmity toward him? He said: I was present with them when their nobles gathered one day in al-Hijr; then he mentioned the like of the hadith of al-Awzai."
"14248","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym from Sufyan from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from the breasts of people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when He leaves no scholar, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14249","Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi from Amr ibn Marzuq from Shu'ba from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Allah, mighty and majestic, does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by its scholar, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14250","Narrated Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madani and Abd al-Rahman ibn Jum'a al-Ladhiqi who said: Narrated Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah al-Uwaysi from Malik; and narrated Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri from Ahmad ibn Salih who said: I read to Abdullah ibn Nafi from Malik ibn Anas from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Abdullah ibn Amr informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, mighty and majestic, does not snatch knowledge from people by snatching, but He takes away the scholars and takes away knowledge with their taking, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14251","Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani from his father from Zuhayr from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14252","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from Abu Salih Abdullah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Muhammad ibn Ajlan from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, does not snatch knowledge by snatching it from them after He gave it to them, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars; and when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders whom they ask for fatwa, and they give them fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14253","Narrated Sulayman ibn al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman from his father from al-Qasim ibn Ma'n from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from the breasts of people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when He leaves no scholar, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14254","Narrated Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi from Abdullah ibn Maslama al-Qa'nabi from his father from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when He leaves no scholar, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14255","Narrated Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani from Ismail ibn Abi Uways from his father from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14256","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi from Sufyan from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, mighty and majestic, does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars; and when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14257","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani from Hammad ibn Zayd from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, glorious His mention, does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars with their knowledge, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14258","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Hammad ibn Salama from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah does not take away knowledge..."" and he mentioned the like thereof."
"14259","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali from Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi from Ayyub from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14260","Narrated Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani from Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali from Abd al-Wahhab from Ayyub and Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Allah, mighty and majestic, does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by its scholar, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14261","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father and from Qatada together from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, does not remove knowledge from the breasts of people after He gave it to them, but its departure is the taking of the scholars; and people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and speak without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14262","Narrated Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj from Yaqub ibn Kasib; and narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi who said: Narrated Said ibn Kathir al-Madani from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, freedman of Muzayna, from Safwan ibn Sulaym who said: Hisham ibn Urwa said; Urwa said; Abdullah ibn Amr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when He leaves no scholar, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14263","Narrated Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi from Malik ibn al-Khalil Abu Ghassan al-Yuhmadi from Muhammad ibn Abi Adi from Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from his grandfather from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, mighty and majestic, does not take away knowledge by snatching it, but He takes away the scholars, so there come to be ignorant leaders for people; and they are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14264","Narrated Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi from Amr ibn Marzuq from Za'ida from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah does not take away knowledge..."" and he mentioned the like thereof."
"14265","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn al-Harish al-Ahwazi from Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani from Rawh ibn Ubada from Ibn Jurayj from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah does not take away knowledge..."" and he mentioned the like thereof."
"14266","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr from his father from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah does not take away knowledge..."" and he mentioned the like thereof."
"14267","Narrated Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Yazid al-Hawti from Abu al-Mughira from al-Awzai from Hisham from his father from Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Allah does not take away knowledge..."" and he mentioned the like thereof."
"14268","Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab from Abu al-Mughira from al-Awzai from Hisham ibn Urwa from Abdullah, and he did not mention Urwa, and he mentioned the hadith."
"14269","Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl from Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith."
"14270","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Urwa from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, glorious His mention, does not snatch knowledge from people after He gave it to them, but He takes away the scholars; every time a scholar goes, what he had of knowledge goes with him, until there remain those who do not know, and they go astray and lead astray."""
"14271","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, does not take away knowledge with a taking by which He takes it, but He takes away the scholars with their knowledge, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders, and they are asked and narrate, so they go astray and lead astray."""
"14272","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan from Abu al-Tahir Ibn al-Sarh from Ismail ibn Abi Uways from Malik ibn Anas from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Satan comes to one of you and says: Who created the sky? And he says: Allah; and he says: Who created the earth? And he says: Allah; and he says: Who created Allah? So when one of you finds that, let him say: I believe in Allah and His Messenger."""
"14273","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from al-Hakam ibn Musa from Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and sees better than it, let him expiate for his oath and do that which is better."""
"14274","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Abdan ibn Ahmad who said: Narrated Uqba ibn Mukram from Yunus ibn Bukayr from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not pray in the resting places of camels, and pray in the resting places of sheep."""
"14275","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from al-Qa'nabi from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Isa ibn Talha from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in the Farewell Pilgrimage at Mina while they asked him; and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, unknowingly I shaved before I sacrificed?! And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sacrifice, and no harm""; and another man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, unknowingly I sacrificed before I stoned?! He said: ""Stone, and no harm""; he said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not asked about anything done early or late but he said: ""Do, and no harm."""
"14276","Narrated Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Shibami from Abd al-Razzaq from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Isa ibn Talha from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, and he mentioned the like thereof."
"14277","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abdullah ibn Raja from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama from al-Zuhri from Isa ibn Talha from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: I was present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the jamra while he was being asked; and a man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I sacrificed before I stoned?! He said: ""Stone, and no harm""; and another man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before I sacrificed?! He said: ""Sacrifice, and no harm""; he said: And he was not asked about anything done early or late but he said: ""Do, and no harm."""
"14278","Narrated Bishr ibn Musa from al-Humaydi from Sufyan from al-Zuhri who said: I heard Isa ibn Talha narrating from Abdullah ibn Amr that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before I stoned?! He said: ""Stone, and no harm""; another said: I shaved before I slaughtered?! And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Slaughter, and no harm."""
"14279","Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi from Abdullah ibn Salih from al-Layth from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir from Ibn Shihab from Isa ibn Talha from Abdullah ibn Amr that he heard men asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for fatwa in the Farewell Pilgrimage; and a man says: I did not know that stoning is before sacrifice, so I sacrificed before I stoned?! And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Then stone, and no harm""; and some of them said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not know that sacrifice is before shaving, so I shaved before I sacrificed?! And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Then sacrifice, and no harm."""
"14280","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Misri from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah al-Munkadiri from Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk from Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Qays from his father from Musa ibn Uqba from al-Zuhri from Isa ibn Talha from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""O people, take your rites, for I do not know; perhaps I shall not perform Hajj after this year of mine."""
"14281","Narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi from Abdullah ibn Imran from Abu Dawud from Zam'a ibn Salih from al-Zuhri from Isa ibn Talha from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing upon his mount at Mina."
"14282","Narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi from Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail from Abd al-Salam ibn Harb from Abu Khalid al-Dalani from Amr ibn Murra from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Abu Kathir al-Zubaydi from Abdullah ibn Amr, raised (to the Prophet), who said: ""Chairs of light will be placed for the believers, and the cloud will shade them, and that day will be upon them like an hour of daytime."""
"14283","Narrated Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti from Abu Nuaym from Sufyan from al-A'mash from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ziyad from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Abdullah ibn Amr that he said on the day of Siffin: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say regarding Ammar: ""The rebellious party will kill him""; and Mu'awiya said: You keep slipping in your urine! Did we kill him?! Those who brought him are the ones who killed him."
"14284","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Ubayd ibn Asbat ibn Muhammad from his father from al-A'mash from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ziyad from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr and Amr ibn al-As and Mu'awiya say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ammar: ""The rebellious party will kill you."""
"14285","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama from Muhammad ibn Sudran from Muhammad ibn Abi Adi from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar from al-Zuhri from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: There were people at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disputing about the Quran, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day with his face changed, and said: ""O people, by this the nations were destroyed; and the Quran confirms part of it with part, so do not belie part of it with part."""
"14286","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari from Makki ibn Ibrahim from Musa ibn Ubayda al-Rabadhi from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As; and from Abu Hazim from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Before Allah are seventy thousand veils of light and darkness; and no soul hears anything of the sound of those veils but it perishes."""
"14287","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari from Raja ibn Muhammad al-Udhri from Abdullah ibn Humran from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar from his father from Umar ibn al-Hakam from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: A man entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was distributing gold ore, and said: O Muhammad, be just! He said: ""Woe to you, and who will be just if I am not just?! And with whom is justice sought after me?!"" Then he said: ""It is near that there will come a people like this one asking by the Book of Allah while they are its enemies; they recite the Book of Allah with shaven heads; and when they come out, strike their necks."""
"14288","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Said ibn Sulayman from Ishaq ibn Sulayman from Musa ibn Ubayda from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Disputation about the Quran is disbelief."""
"14289","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud from Khalid ibn Nizar from Hisham ibn Sad from Said ibn Abi Hilal from Rabi'a ibn Sayf from Iyad ibn Uqba al-Fihri from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no Muslim who dies on the day of Friday or the night of Friday but Allah protects him from the trial of the grave."""
"14290","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abu Hatim Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Baghdadi who said: Narrated Muhammad ibn Zanbur from Muhammad ibn Jabir from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we heard wailing; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Go and see what this is?"" He said: It is Abdullah ibn Rawaha, he died! He said: ""He has not died""; and he recovered, for he had fainted; and he was informed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was coming to him, so he met him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I fainted and the women cried out: O my support! O my mountain! And an angel with him holding an iron mace placed it between his legs and said: Do you say as these say? I said: No; and had I said yes, he would have struck me with it."
"14291","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from his father from Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym from Isa, I think of the people of Madina, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Salama, or Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""He has succeeded who embraced Islam and whose provision was sufficiency and was patient with it."""
"14292","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sawti from Affan from Shu'ba from Sad ibn Ibrahim from Hilal ibn Talha, or Talha ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fasting three days is the fast of the whole year: 'Whoever brings a good deed shall have ten like it'""; I said: I can bear more than that; and he said: ""Fast the fast of Dawud; he used to fast a day and break fast a day."""
"14293","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from his father from Rawh ibn Ubada from Malik ibn Anas from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad from a freedman of Abdullah ibn Amr from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man's prayer sitting is half his prayer standing."""
"14294","Narrated Abu Shuayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani from Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani from Muhammad ibn Salama from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir from Ismail, freedman of Abdullah ibn Amr, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the killing of the believer is greater with Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the passing away of the world."""
"14295","Narrated Ali ibn Said al-Razi from Abdullah ibn Imran al-Asbahani from Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi from Abu Sinan from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Shuayb ibn Abdullah ibn Amr from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The world is sweet and green; and whoever takes it with its right, it is blessed for him in it; and many a one plunging into what his soul desires shall have nothing on the Day of Resurrection but the Fire."""
"14296","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal from Hammad ibn Salama from Thabit al-Bunani from Shuayb ibn Abdullah ibn Amr from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Fast a day and for you are ten days""; he said: Increase me, O Messenger of Allah; he said: ""Fast two days and for you are nine days""; he said: Increase me, O Messenger of Allah; he said: ""Fast three days, and for you are eight days""; he said: And I informed Mutarrif of that, and he said: I see only that deed is increased and reward is decreased."
"14297","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq from Abda ibn Abi Lubaba from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu Abdullah, freedman of Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: Abdullah ibn Amr said while circumambulating the House: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in these days: ""There are no days in which deeds are more beloved to Allah than in these days""; and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad in the path of Allah? He said: ""Not even jihad in the path of Allah, except one who went out with himself and his wealth then did not return until his blood was shed."" Yahya said: And I met Habib ibn Abi Thabit and asked him, and he narrated the like of this; and it was said to Yahya: Did he differ from him? He said: No; and he narrated to me that they are the ten days."
"14298","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Hudba ibn Khalid from Hammad ibn al-Ja'd from Qatada from Ata ibn Abi Rabah that a freedman of Abdullah ibn Amr narrated to him from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Whoever circumambulates this House seven times and prays two rak'as behind the Maqam of Ibrahim, upon him be peace, it equals a freed slave."""
"14299","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i from Yaqub ibn Abi Abbad; and narrated Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami from Ahmad ibn Yunus who said: Narrated Ya'la ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi from Bakr ibn Wa'il who said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from a freedman of Abdullah ibn Amr from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: Pain spread in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and many prayed sitting; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."""
"14300","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim Abu al-Nu'man from Raja Abu Yahya, companion of al-Saqat, from Musafi ibn Shayba from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I bear witness by Allah that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The Corner and the Maqam are two rubies from the rubies of Paradise whose light Allah effaced; and were it not for what Allah effaced of their light, they would illuminate what is between the east and the west."""
"14301","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Arim Abu al-Nu'man; and narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Abu Umar al-Darir and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi; and narrated Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi from Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' who said: Narrated Abu Awana from Abu Bishr from Yusuf ibn Mahak from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the Asr prayer pressed us, and we performed ablution and began wiping over our feet; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out, or the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Woe to the heels from the Fire."""
"14302","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yahya ibn Said from Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas from al-Walid ibn Abdullah from Yusuf ibn Mahak from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I used to write down everything I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking to memorize it, and Quraysh forbade me and said: Do you write down everything you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is a human who speaks in anger and pleasure! So I refrained from writing, and I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he pointed with his finger to his mouth and said: ""Write, for by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, nothing comes out of it but truth."""
"14303","Narrated Idris ibn Jafar from Yazid ibn Harun; and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym who said: Narrated Mis'ar from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu al-Abbas from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his permission for jihad, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Are your parents alive?"" He said: Yes; he said: ""Then in them strive."""
"14304","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Abdan ibn Ahmad who said: Narrated Asim ibn al-Nadr from Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman from his father from Mis'ar from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu al-Abbas from Abdullah ibn Amr that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking jihad and emigration, and informed him that he had two parents; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Then in them strive."""
"14305","Narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar from Muhammad ibn Kathir from Sufyan from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu al-Abbas from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I seek jihad; he said: ""Are your parents alive?"" He said: Yes; he said: ""Then in them strive."""
"14306","Narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn A'yan from Ali ibn al-Ja'd from Shu'ba from Habib ibn Abi Thabit that Abu al-Abbas al-Makki said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his permission for jihad, and he said: ""Are your parents alive?"" He said: Yes; he said: ""Then in them strive."" He is Abu al-Abbas the poet, and his name is al-Sa'ib ibn Farrukh, and it is said: al-Hajjaj ibn Farrukh."
"14307","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Yahya ibn Said from Sufyan and Shu'ba who said: Narrated Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu al-Abbas from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I seek jihad; and he said: ""Are your parents alive?"" He said: Yes; he said: ""Then in them strive."""
"14308","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym from Sufyan from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu al-Abbas from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""He has not fasted who fasts perpetually."""
"14309","Narrated Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi from Sufyan from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu al-Abbas from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The most beloved fasting to Allah is the fast of Dawud; he fasts a day and breaks fast a day, and does not flee when he meets (the enemy)."""
"14310","Narrated Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti from Wahb ibn Baqiyya from Khalid from Mutarrif ibn Tarif from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu al-Abbas from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Have I not been informed that you stand at night and fast the day?"" I said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah, and I intended by that only good. He said: ""Do not do so; for when you do that, the eye grows weary and the soul grows satiated; and he has not fasted who fasts perpetually; but I guide you to the fast of the whole year: three days of every month, and that is the fast of the whole year."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, I can bear more than that. He said: ""Then fast five of the month""; I said: I can bear more than that; he said: ""Then fast the fast of Dawud, for he used to fast a day and break fast a day, and does not flee when he meets (the enemy)."""
"14311","Narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati from al-Rabi ibn Yahya al-Ushnani from Shu'ba from Amr ibn Dinar from Abu al-Abbas from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Recite the Quran in five (days)."""
"14312","Narrated Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar from Yazid ibn Harun from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Abu al-Zubayr from Abu al-Abbas from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: Mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were a people striving hard in worship with severe striving, and he said: ""That is the ardor of Islam and its zeal; and for every zeal is a lull; and whoever's lull is toward moderation, then excellent is he; and whoever's lull is toward disobedience, those are the destroyed."""
"14313","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Ali ibn al-Madini from Hisham ibn Yusuf from Ibn Jurayj from Amr ibn Dinar from Amr ibn Aws from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""The most beloved fasting to Allah is the fast of Dawud; he used to fast half the year; and the most beloved prayer to Allah is the prayer of Dawud; he used to sleep half the night and stand, then sleep its end, then stand a third of the night after its half."""
"14314","Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Abd al-Razzaq from Ibn Uyayna from Amr ibn Dinar from Salim from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: Over the baggage of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a man called Karkara."
"14315","Narrated Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj from Yahya ibn Bukayr from Ibn Wahb from Abd al-Rahman ibn Salman from Uqayl ibn Khalid from Amr ibn Shuayb that Shuayb and Mujahid narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Amr narrated to them; he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I retain your hadith and aid myself with my hand? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes""; I said: O Messenger of Allah, in anger and pleasure? He said: ""Yes; for I say nothing but truth."""
"14316","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Asim ibn Ali from Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talha ibn Ubaydullah from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: There were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) some people of his Companions, and I was with them, and I was the youngest of the people; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire""; and when the people went out I said: How do you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when you heard what he said? And you plunge into narrating hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And they laughed and said: O son of our brother, all that we heard from him is with us in a book."
"14317","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Asim ibn Ali from Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talha from Mujahid who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: Mu'awiya sought to take some of his wealth, so he gathered his sons and said to them: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever is wronged of his wealth and fights for it and is killed, he is a martyr."""
"14318","Narrated Abdullah ibn Musa ibn Abi Uthman al-Anmati from Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmala from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Kinship is attached to the Throne; and the one who maintains ties is not the one who reciprocates, but the one who maintains ties is the one who joins it when his kinship is cut."""
"14319","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi from Sufyan from Dawud ibn Shabur from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Jibril, upon him be peace, kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would have him inherit."""
"14320","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi from Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi from Sufyan from Dawud ibn Shabur from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take the Quran from four: two men of the Emigrants and two men of the Ansar: from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and Salim, freedman of Abu Hudhayfa, and Ubayy ibn Ka'b and Mu'adh ibn Jabal."" He said: And he singled out Abdullah ibn Mas'ud with a word; he said: ""Whoever wishes to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite as Ibn Umm Abd recites."""
"14321","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from his father from Muhammad ibn Salama from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from al-Mughira ibn Hakim from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I hear from you things in anger; shall I write them? He said: ""Yes; for I say nothing in anger and pleasure but truth."""
"14322","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz from Abu Zayd al-Nahwi Said ibn Aws from Shu'ba from al-Hakam who said: I heard Mujahid say: Mu'awiya sought to attribute Junada ibn Abi Umayya, a man of al-Azd, to himself, and Abdullah ibn Amr said to him, I heard it and he raised it; he said: ""Whoever claims (descent) to other than his father will not find the fragrance of Paradise, though its fragrance is found from a distance of seventy years""; and when that reached Junada he said: O Commander of the Believers, I am but an arrow of your quiver, so shoot me wherever you wish."
"14323","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Rawh ibn Ubada from Shu'ba from al-Hakam from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"14324","Narrated Jafar ibn Ahmad al-Shami from Abu Kurayb from Firdaws ibn al-Ash'ari from Mas'ud ibn Sulayman from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Mujahid from Junada ibn Abi Umayya from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever claims (descent) to other than his father will not find the comfort of Paradise, though it is found from a journey of seventy years."""
"14325","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Said ibn Sulayman from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad from al-A'mash from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was praying sitting, and said: ""Know that the prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."""
"14326","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Khallad ibn Yazid from Sharik from al-A'mash from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah, I ask You for a pure life, and an upright death, and a return that is not disgraceful."""
"14327","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Humayd ibn Mas'ada from Husayn ibn Numayr from Husayn, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: Disliked are the dowry of the prostitute, and the fee of the soothsayer, and the earning of the cupper, and the price of the dog."
"14328","Narrated Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinna'i from Muhammad ibn Jami' al-Attar from Husayn ibn Numayr from Husayn from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""The expiation of the gathering is: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; I bear witness that there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You."""
"14329","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Shu'ba from Husayn from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""For every worker is a lull, and for every lull is a zeal; and whoever's lull is toward my Sunna has succeeded."""
"14330","Narrated Jafar ibn Ahmad al-Shami from Abu Kurayb from Firdaws ibn al-Ash'ari from Mas'ud ibn Sulayman from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said regarding the Dajjal: Whatever is made dubious to you of him, then Allah, mighty and majestic, is not one-eyed; he will come out and remain in the earth forty mornings, passing every watering place but the Ka'ba and Bayt al-Maqdis and Madina; the month is like Friday and Friday is like the day; and with him are a garden and a fire, and his fire is a garden and his garden is a fire; with him is a mountain of bread and a river of water; he calls a man whom Allah gives him power over none but him, and says: What do you say of me? And he says: You are the enemy of Allah, and you are the lying Dajjal; and he calls for a saw and places it at his head and splits him until he falls upon the earth, then revives him, and says: What do you say of me? And he says: By Allah, I was never more clear-sighted about you than I am now; you are the enemy of Allah, the Dajjal of whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us; he said: And he raises his sword to him but cannot harm him, and says: Keep him away from me."
"14331","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb from Mu'awiya ibn Hisham from Sufyan from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."""
"14332","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi from Mu'awiya ibn Amr from Za'ida from Layth from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Be upright, and you will never encompass; and know that among the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution but a believer."""
"14333","Narrated Ahmad ibn Ziyad ibn Zakariyya al-Ansari from Yazid ibn Qays from al-Mu'afa ibn Imran al-Tuhawi from Ismail ibn Ayyash from Jafar ibn al-Harith from Layth from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Be upright, and you will never encompass; and know that among the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution but a believer."""
"14334","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati from Abu Musa al-Harawi Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus from Layth from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah will fill your hands with the non-Arabs, and they will become lions who do not flee; and they will strike your necks and take your spoils."""
"14335","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from his father from Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman from Layth; and narrated Mahmud ibn al-Faraj al-Asbahani from Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali from Sufyan from Layth from Mujahid who said: When Ammar ibn Yasir was killed, Abdullah ibn Amr said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The rebellious party will kill him""; and Mu'awiya said: Did we kill him?! Those who brought him forth are the ones who killed him."
"14336","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Ahmad ibn Abda from Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakka'i from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Be upright, and you will never encompass; and know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution but a believer."""
"14337","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad from Khalid from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr, raised, who said: ""Whoever drinks wine and puts it in his belly, his prayer will not be accepted for seven (days); and if he dies he dies a disbeliever; and if he drinks it until it overcomes him from something of the obligations, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days; and if he dies he dies a disbeliever."""
"14338","Narrated Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Massisi from al-Musayyib ibn Wadih from Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ammar: ""The rebellious party will kill you."""
"14339","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Nuaym; and narrated Bishr ibn Musa from Khallad ibn Yahya who said: Narrated Fitr ibn Khalifa from Mujahid Abu al-Hajjaj who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Kinship is attached to the Throne; and the one who maintains ties is not the one who reciprocates, but the one who maintains ties is the one who joins his kinship when it is cut."""
"14340","Narrated Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar from Muhammad ibn Kathir from Sufyan from al-A'mash and al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi and Fitr from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr; Sufyan said: Sulayman did not raise it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and al-Hasan and Fitr raised it; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one who maintains ties is not the one who reciprocates, but the one who maintains ties is the one who joins his kinship when it is cut."""
"14341","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh from his father from Marwan ibn Mu'awiya from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like thereof."
"14342","Narrated Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi from Sufyan from al-Hasan ibn Amr from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""The one who maintains ties is not the one who reciprocates, but the one who maintains ties is the one who joins his kinship when it is cut."""
"14343","Narrated Ali ibn Said al-Razi from Abd al-Rahman ibn Salama al-Razi from Salama ibn al-Fadl from Sufyan al-Thawri from Zubayd from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one who maintains ties is not the one who reciprocates, but the one who maintains ties is the one who joins his kinship when it is cut."""
"14344","Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad from Ismail ibn Zakariyya al-Kufi from Fudayl ibn Iyad from Fitr from Hammad from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one who maintains ties is not the one who reciprocates, but the one who maintains ties is the one who joins his kinship when it is cut."""
"14345","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sawti from Affan from Abu Awana from Mughira ibn Miqsam from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: My father married me to a woman of lineage, and he used to visit his daughter-in-law and ask her about her husband, saying: How is your husband? And she would say: An excellent man of a man who has not trodden our bed nor uncovered her privacy; and when that grew long upon him, he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with him and I met him with him, and he said to me: ""Do you fast?"" I said: I fast every day; he said: ""And how do you complete (the Quran)?"" I said: Every day; and he said: ""Recite it once in every month and fast three days""; I said: I can bear more than that; he said: ""Then break fast two days and fast a day""; I said: I can bear more than that; he said: ""Then fast the fast of Dawud; he used to fast a day and break fast a day, and recite the Quran in every seven."" And he used to say after he grew old and weak: Would that I had accepted the concession of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! And he used to recite the seven (portions) with his family in the day to gather strength for the night, to be lighter upon him; and when he wished to break fast he would break fast days and count them, then fast their number, to come upon what he had parted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon."
"14346","Narrated Musa ibn Hazim al-Asbahani from Muhammad ibn Bukayr al-Hadrami from Marwan ibn Mu'awiya al-Fazari from al-Hasan ibn Amr from Mujahid from Junada ibn Abi Umayya from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Whoever kills a slain person of the dhimmis will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, though its fragrance is found from a journey of a hundred years."""
"14347","Narrated Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari from Said ibn Sulayman from al-Yaman ibn al-Mughira from Abd al-Karim from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever prays four before Asr, Allah forbids him to the Fire."""
"14348","Narrated Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi from Sufyan from Zubayd from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibril kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would have him inherit."""
"14349","Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jammal al-Asbahani from Ismail ibn Yazid al-Qattan from Ibrahim ibn Rustum from Qays ibn al-Rabi from Salim al-Aftas from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The mu'adhdhin who seeks reward is like the martyr wallowing in his blood; when he dies he does not putrefy in his grave."""
"14350","Narrated Uthman ibn Amr al-Dabbi from Abdullah ibn Raja from Za'ida from Layth from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Be upright, and you will never encompass; and know that among the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution but a believer."""
"14351","Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal al-Harrani from Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli from Muhammad ibn Salama from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Dhu al-Suwayqatayn of the Abyssinians will destroy the Ka'ba."""
"14352","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Marzuq al-Mawardi al-Basri from Ubaydullah ibn A'isha from al-Nadr ibn Ismail al-Bajali from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you see my nation fearing the oppressor to say to him: You are an oppressor, then they have been left without support."""
"14353","Narrated Ali ibn Said al-Razi from al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysara al-Razi from Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra from Musa al-Juhani from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara al-Zarrad from Mujahid that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will enter the Fire from the people of this qibla those whose number none but Allah counts, for disobeying Allah and daring against disobeying Him and opposing His obedience; and I shall be permitted intercession, and I shall praise Allah prostrating as I praise Him standing; and it will be said: Raise your head, ask and you shall be given, and intercede and your intercession shall be accepted."""
"14354","Narrated Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk from Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban Mushkudanah from Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman from Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhajir from his father from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""It is not lawful to rent them out nor their quarters, meaning Makka."""
"14355","Narrated Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal from his father and Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki who said: Narrated Sufyan from Amr ibn Dinar from Abu Qabus from Abdullah ibn Amr, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""The merciful will be shown mercy by al-Rahman; show mercy to those on earth and those in heaven will show mercy to you."""
"14356","Narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, my father and Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki told me, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Qabus, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, attributing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The womb (tie of kinship) is a branch from al-Rahman; whoever joins it, it joins him, and whoever cuts it, it cuts him off."
"14357","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father told me, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, Sa'id ibn Kathir informed me that Ja'far ibn al-Muttalib informed him that Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As visited Amr ibn al-As during the days of Mina, and he invited him to lunch, but he said: I am fasting; then a second time and he said the same, then a third time and he said: I am fasting, unless you heard something from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — meaning the prohibition. He said: I did hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14358","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, saying: Abd Allah ibn Amr prepared to fight in defence of al-Waht, and said: Why should I not fight in its defence when I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."
"14359","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: One killed defending his property is a martyr."
"14360","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One killed defending his property is a martyr."
"14361","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la al-San'ani narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Hatim ibn Abi Sagheerah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."
"14362","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abu Yunus al-Qushayri, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abd Allah ibn Safwan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fights defending his property and is killed is a martyr."
"14363","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The one who sits in prayer has half the reward of the one who stands."
"14364","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the bequest of Nuh to his son was: O my son, I enjoin upon you two traits and forbid you two traits. I enjoin upon you the testimony that there is no god but Allah, for if the heavens and the earth were in one scale and it were in the other scale, it would outweigh them; and I enjoin upon you glorification (tasbih), for it is the worship of creation, and magnification (takbir). And I forbid you two traits: pride and arrogance. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is it pride to ride a fine mount? He said: No. I said: Is it pride to wear a fine garment? He said: No. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then what is pride? He said: To belittle the truth and despise people."
"14365","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami said: We were present with Ali at Siffin, and we had assigned two men to his horse; whenever a man became heedless, Ali would spur his horse and find himself amid the enemy camp, then return to us with his sword dyed with blood, saying as he returned: O my companions, excuse me, excuse me! And when we made truce, these would enter the camp of those and those would enter the camp of these. Ammar ibn Yasir was a banner for the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Ammar would not take any valley of the valleys of Siffin without the companions of Muhammad following him. We reached Hashim ibn Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas with the banner planted, and he said: What is wrong with you, Hashim — one-eyed and cowardly?! There is no good in a one-eyed man who does not face hardship. So Hashim seized the banner, saying: The one-eyed one striving... Ammar said to him: Advance, for Paradise is beneath the flashing blades; the wide-eyed houris have adorned themselves, with Muhammad and his party in the highest company! So they both charged and did not return until they were both killed. And when we made truce, these would enter the camp of those and those would enter the camp of these. Then I looked and saw four men walking: Mu'awiyah, Abu al-A'war al-Sulami, Amr ibn al-As and his son. I said to myself: If I stay to the right of two of them I will not hear their speech, so I chose to spur my horse and split between them; I did so, placing two on my right and two on my left, and I began listening sometimes to Mu'awiyah and Abu al-A'war, and sometimes to Amr ibn al-As and his son Abd Allah ibn Amr. I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say to his father: O father, we have killed this man, about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said what he said! He said: Which man? He said: Ammar ibn Yasir. Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day the mosque was built, when we were carrying one brick at a time while Ammar carried two bricks at a time, and he passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You carry two bricks at a time while you are sweating?! Yet the rebellious party will kill you, and you are of the people of Paradise. Then I heard Amr say to Mu'awiyah: We have killed this man, about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said what he said! He said: Which man? He said: Ammar ibn Yasir. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day the mosque was built, when we were carrying one brick at a time while Ammar carried two bricks at a time, and he passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: O Abu al-Yaqzan, do you carry two bricks while you are sweating?! Yet the rebellious party will kill you, and you are of the people of Paradise. Mu'awiyah said: Be quiet! By Allah, you keep slipping in your urine! Did we kill him?! Those who brought him and cast him between our spears are the ones who killed him. Then they called out in Mu'awiyah's camp: Ammar was only killed by those who brought him."
"14366","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abd Allah ibn Amr, do you fast the day and stand the night? I said: Yes. He said: If you do that, the eyes will grow heavy and the soul will weary. Your eye has a right over you, your body has a right over you, and your family has a right over you. So stand and sleep, fast and break your fast. Fast three days of every month, for that is the fast of a lifetime. I said: I am stronger than that. He said: None fasts who fasts perpetually; but if you must, then fast the fast of the Messenger of Allah, Dawud: he would fast a day and break a day, and he would not flee when he met (the enemy)."
"14367","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus informed us, al-Awza'i al-Azdi said: Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None fasts who fasts perpetually."
"14368","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mu'ammal narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I bind knowledge? He said: Yes. I said: And what is its binding? He said: Writing."
"14369","Abd Allah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, in marfu' form, who said: There is no creature, bird or otherwise, killed without right except that it will dispute him on the Day of Resurrection."
"14370","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Umar ibn Hawshab informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Not of us are women who imitate men, nor men who imitate women."
"14371","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father told me, saying: I found in my father's book in his handwriting: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fights defending his property and is killed is a martyr."
"14372","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ismah al-Nasibi informed us, Hamzah ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Any woman married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is void; if he has consummated with her, she is entitled to her dowry for what he made lawful of her private part, and they are separated; if he has not consummated with her, they are separated; and the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"14373","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, Marzuq Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The most beloved prayer to Allah is the prayer of Dawud (peace be upon him): he would pray half the night and sleep the remaining half; so he would pray two-thirds of it and sleep one-third of it."
"14374","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Compeller takes His heavens and His earth in His Hand and closes His Hand — and he began closing and opening it — then says: I am the Compeller, I am the King! Where are the tyrants?! Where are the arrogant?! He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swayed to his right and to his left, until I saw the pulpit shaking from its lowest part, so that I was saying: Will it fall with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?! So Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated it from Ibn Abi Hazim, saying: from Abd Allah ibn Amr; and others narrated it from him, saying: from Ibn Umar."
"14375","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla told me, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: Jibril conducted Ibrahim (peace be upon them both) to Mina, and led him in Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha and Fajr at Mina, then went with him from Mina to Arafat in the morning and led him in the two prayers, then stood until the sun set, then brought him to Muzdalifah and alighted there and spent the night there, then stood and prayed as promptly as any Muslim prays, then brought him as slowly as any Muslim prays, then moved him on to Mina, where he stoned, sacrificed and shaved; then Allah revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Follow the religion of Ibrahim, inclining to truth, and he was not of the polytheists."
"14376","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, that a Bedouin came to Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As and said: I am weak with riding animals, and I have pebbles with me; may I depart from Jam' before the imam departs? He said: Ibrahim (peace be upon him) prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha and Fajr at Mina; when morning came he went to Arafah and stood, then departed from Arafah and spent the night at Jam', and when it was the hastened prayer he prayed Fajr then stood, and when it was the brightened prayer he departed; and your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to follow the religion of your father Ibrahim."
"14377","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us. And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, both saying: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, saying: A man came to Abd Allah ibn Amr and said: I am weak with riding animals and weak with family; do you see that I should hasten? Abd Allah ibn Amr said to him: Ibrahim (peace be upon him) came and circumambulated the House, and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then went and prayed Zuhr at Mina; when the next day came, at sunrise he went in the morning to the station at Arafah, then went and stood at Arafah until the sun set, then departed and prayed at Jam' and spent the night there; when the next day came he prayed the hastened prayer, then stood until the morning prayer; and Allah revealed to your Prophet to follow the religion of Ibrahim, inclining to truth, and he was not of the polytheists."
"14378","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, my father told me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to him: Have you gathered the Qur'an (memorized it)? I said: Yes. He said: Read it every month. I said: I find energy. He said: Then in twenty days. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I find strength! I kept on until he said: Read it in seven days. Then I wished I had accepted what he said: Read it in a month."
"14379","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mu'ammal narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that he wore a ring of gold, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at it as though he disliked it; so he put on with it a ring of iron, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at it and said: This is worse and worse. So he threw it away and wore a ring of silver, and he remained silent."
"14380","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us. And Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Attar narrated to us, both saying: Nafi' ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: Abd Allah ibn Amr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Basin is a month's journey; its corners are equal; its water is whiter than silver leaf, its scent sweeter than musk, and its cups like the stars of the sky; whoever drinks from it will never thirst."
"14381","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ubayd Allah al-Muqri narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ubayd Allah al-Madani narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah say: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The fasting person at his breaking of the fast has a supplication that is not rejected."
"14382","Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abbadani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us. And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, Suhayb al-Hadhdha said: from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a sparrow without its right, Allah will question him about it on the Day of Resurrection."
"14383","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father told me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Suhayb, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever slaughters a sparrow or kills it for nothing — Amr said: and I think he said: except by its right — Allah will question him about it on the Day of Resurrection."
"14384","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, Sulayman al-Ahwal informed me that Thabit, the freedman of Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman, informed him, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed over his property is a martyr."
"14385","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, Abu al-Aswad told me, from Ikrimah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed defending his property, wronged, Paradise is his."
"14386","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Bujayr ibn Abi Bujayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog that is neither a hunting dog nor a livestock dog, his reward decreases by a qirat every day. Then he mentioned that they were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and they passed by the grave of Abu Righal and said: What is this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: This is the grave of Abu Righal, the father of Thaqif; he was a man of Thamud, and his dwelling was at the Sanctuary; when Allah destroyed his people with what He destroyed them, his place in the Sanctuary protected him; but he went out until, when he reached here, he died and was buried, and buried with him was a branch of gold. So we hastened to it and dug it out."
"14387","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Bujayr ibn Abi Bujayr, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: When we went out to al-Ta'if and passed by a grave, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the grave of Abu Righal, the father of Thaqif; he was of Thamud, and he was in this Sanctuary so he was shielded from it; but when he left it, the punishment that befell his people befell him at this place, and he was buried in it; and the sign of that is that a branch of gold was buried with him — if you dig it up you will find it. So the people hastened to it and dug out the branch from it."
"14388","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating from Yahya ibn Hakim ibn Safwan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: I gathered the Qur'an and read it in one night, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I fear the time will grow long upon you and you will weary; read it in a month. I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and my youth! He said: Read it in twenty. I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and my youth! He said: Read it in ten. I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and my youth! He said: Read it in seven. I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me enjoy my strength and my youth! But he refused."
"14389","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Sayf ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr, Abu al-Zubayr told me, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see my nation fearing the wrongdoer, to say: You are a wrongdoer, then they have been forsaken."
"14390","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Makki narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Tawus, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw two saffron-dyed garments on me and said: Did your mother command you with these? He said: I said: Shall I wash them? He said: Rather, burn them both."
"14391","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Wasiti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is imminent that devils whom Sulayman ibn Dawud had bound in the sea will appear among you; they will pray with you in your mosques, recite the Qur'an with you, and dispute with you about religion, yet they are devils in the form of men."
"14392","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ziyad ibn Siminkush, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There will be a tribulation that utterly consumes the Arabs; its slain are in the Fire; the tongue in it strikes harder than the sword."
"14393","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of the people of the Fire will appear before you from this mountain pass. I had left my father performing ablution, and I feared it might be him; then a man other than him appeared, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is this one."
"14394","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, who said: I heard a man narrating to Ibn Abbas, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will surely appear before you who will be raised on the Day of Resurrection upon other than my practice — or: other than my religion. I had left my father at home, and I feared it might be him; then another appeared, and he said: It is this one."
"14395","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw two saffron-dyed garments on me and said: They are of the garments of the people of the Fire, so do not wear them."
"14396","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): In how long is the Qur'an to be read? He said: In forty. He said: I can do more than that. He said: In a month. He said: I can do more than that. He said: In fifteen. Then he said: In ten. Then he said: In seven. Then he did not go below seven."
"14397","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Umar informed us. And Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Umar narrated to us, Bishr ibn Asim told me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah hates the eloquent man who rolls his tongue as the cow rolls its tongue."
"14398","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ata narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever drinks wine, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights; if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance; if he drinks it again, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights; if he drinks it again, it becomes due upon Allah to give him to drink from the mud of al-Khabal. He said: And what is the mud of al-Khabal? He said: The pus of the people of the Fire."
"14399","Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Nafi' ibn Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: This verse was revealed concerning Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt: The one to whom We gave Our signs, but he detached himself from them."
"14400","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from his father, from Urwah ibn Iyad, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter Paradise in whose heart is a mustard seed's weight of pride."
